        '212.   - Cite the specific similarity and source\n' +
        '213.   - Verify the style guide was applied transformatively, not reproductively\n' +
        '214. \n' +
        '215. Each lens produces a structured findings document with severity levels (critical / major / minor / suggestion). All critical and major findings MUST be addressed in a revision pass before the chapter is considered complete.\n' +
        '216. \n' +
        '217. ### Phase 9: Polish & Delivery\n' +
        '218. - **Final proofread**: Last pass for typos, formatting, consistency\n' +
        '219. - **Chapter summaries**: One-paragraph summary per chapter for easy reference\n' +
        "220. - **Series knowledge base update** (if series): Promote this book's canonical facts into the series knowledge base — see Series Architecture below\n" +
        '221. - **Delivery package**: All output artifacts organized and cross-referenced under the book directory\n' +
        '222. \n' +
        '223. ## Series Architecture & Sequel Production\n' +
        '224. \n' +
        '225. The system MUST be designed for series production from day one, even if the first invocation is a standalone. All generated knowledge is organized to enable seamless sequel creation.\n' +
        '226. \n' +
        '227. ### Artifact Organization\n' +
        '228. \n' +
        '229. Every artifact type that accumulates significant knowledge MUST be decomposed into **subcategory files** within a typed directory. Monolithic files become unnavigable and cause context-window waste — agents loading the world bible to check a single geography detail shouldn\'t need to ingest the entire magic system. Subcategories also make cross-referencing precise (an outline scene can cite `world/magic/blood-singing.md` rather than "see world-bible.md, magic section").\n' +
        '230. \n' +
        '231. ```\n' +
        '232. output/\n' +
        '233.   series.json                    ← Series metadata (title, book count, status)\n' +
        '234.   series/                        ← Series-level canonical knowledge (cross-book truth)\n' +
