      'gen_ai.provider.name': 'github',
      'gen_ai.tool.call.arguments': '{"command":"cd /home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator\\n# Read workflow skill files\\nfor f in shared/skills/workflow/docs/SKILL.md shared/skills/workflow/vscode/SKILL.md shared/skills/xperience/SKILL.md shared/skills/xperience-documentation/SKILL.md; do\\n  if [ -f \\"$f\\" ]; then\\n    echo \\"=== $f ===\\"\\n    head -30 \\"$f\\"\\n    echo -e \\"\\\\n---\\\\n\\"\\n  fi\\ndone\\n","description":"Read workflow and xperience skills","initial_wait":10}',
      'gen_ai.tool.call.result': '=== shared/skills/xperience/SKILL.md ===\n' +
        '---\n' +
        'name: xperience\n' +
        'description: A router skill for working with Xperience by Kentico source code and product internals. Use this skill whenever you need to orient yourself in the CMSSolution codebase, identify which subsystem owns a feature, map documentation topics to source roots, or find the right product area before doing deeper research. Use it for source-structure questions even when the user only mentions a feature name and not the repository layout explicitly.\n' +
        '---\n' +
        '\n' +
        '# Xperience by Kentico Source Map\n' +
        '\n' +
        'This skill maps the major source-code areas under `./resources/repositories/xperience/CMSSolution/`.\n' +
        '\n' +
        'Use it to answer questions like:\n' +
        '\n' +
        '- which subsystem owns this feature\n' +
        '- where a documentation topic maps into product source code\n' +
        '- which root directories matter before doing detailed code search\n' +
        '- how product surfaces relate to each other at a high level\n' +
        '\n' +
        'For documentation-tree orientation rather than source-tree orientation, use the companion `xperience-documentation` skill.\n' +
        '\n' +
        '## Solution and Platform Structure\n' +
        '\n' +
        '- [Solution foundations](references/source-solution-foundations.md) — solution-level build/config anchors plus the shared platform roots such as `Base`, `Core`, `Helpers`, and `Modules`\n' +
        '- [Data, security, and operations](references/source-data-security-operations.md) — `DataEngine`, `DbDataManager`, `DataProtection`, `MacroEngine`, `Scheduler`, `ContinuousIntegration`, `WebFarmSync`, and other horizontal runtime services\n' +
        '- [Integrations and storage](references/source-integrations-and-storage.md) — external integration packages plus the internal file/storage abstraction layer in `IO`\n' +
        '- [Tooling, samples, and tests](references/source-tooling-samples-tests.md) — analyzers, templates, internal tools, samples, and subsystem-oriented test projects\n' +
        '\n' +
        '## Product Surfaces\n' +
        '\n' +
        '- [Content and channels](references/source-content-and-channels.md) — `ContentEngine`, `Websites`, `Headless`, `MediaLibrary`, workflow, sync, and workspaces\n' +
        '- [Admin and web runtime](references/source-admin-and-runtime.md) — `Admin`, `Mvc`, `Routing.Web`, `Membership`, and `AIRA`\n' +
        '- [Marketing and engagement](references/source-marketing-and-engagement.md) — activities, contacts, automation, journeys, email, forms, and online marketing\n' +
        '\n' +
        '---\n' +
        '\n' +
        '=== shared/skills/xperience-documentation/SKILL.md ===\n' +
        '---\n' +
        'name: xperience-documentation\n' +
        'description: A skill that maps the structure of the Xperience by Kentico documentation — what areas exist, what each section covers, how pages relate to each other, and where the corresponding source code lives. Use this skill whenever you need to understand the documentation hierarchy, find where a topic is documented, identify related pages across sections, plan documentation changes, or understand how the docs map to the Xperience source code. This skill is especially important when working on documentation tasks, writing new pages, restructuring existing content, identifying cross-references, or orienting yourself in the kentico-docs-jekyll repository. Use it even when the user just mentions "the docs" or "documentation structure" — it covers both business-user and developer-facing sections comprehensively.\n' +
        '---\n' +
        '\n' +
        '# Xperience by Kentico Documentation Structure\n' +
        '\n' +
        'A reference for the structure and content areas of the Xperience by Kentico documentation, located at `./src/_documentation/_documentation/` in the kentico-docs-jekyll repository.\n' +
        '\n' +
        'The documentation has two main sections: **Business users** (end-user guides for content editors, marketers, and administrators using the Xperience admin UI) and **Developers and admins** (technical guides for developers building on and configuring the platform).\n' +
        '\n' +
        'Each reference below covers one documentation area — its page hierarchy, what each page covers, and where the corresponding source code lives in `./resources/repositories/xperience/CMSSolution/`.\n' +
        '\n' +
        '## Business Users Section\n' +
        '\n' +
        'These references cover the admin UI guides aimed at content editors and marketers.\n' +
        '\n' +
        '- [Content hub](references/business-content-hub.md) — Content items, folders, and content item assets in the Content hub application\n' +
        '- [Website content](references/business-website-content.md) — Pages, page builder, URLs, templates, translations, permissions, and the website content tree\n' +
        '- [Digital marketing](references/business-digital-marketing.md) — Contact management, email campaigns, forms, automation, customer journeys, and widget personalization\n' +
        '- [Media libraries](references/business-media-libraries.md) — Media library creation and file management\n' +
        '- [General features](references/business-general.md) — Headless content, content sync, content versioning, email queue, members, recycle bin, rich text editor, commerce stores, AIRA, and user profiles\n' +
        '\n' +
        '## Developers and Admins Section\n' +
        '\n' +
        '### Development\n' +
        '\n' +
        'Core website and content development guides.\n' +
