        '14. ## Context\n' +
        '15. \n' +
        '16. Check whether `.fractal-factory/` exists:\n' +
        "17. - If it doesn't exist → run `bash fractal-factory-bootstrap.sh` to initialize\n" +
        "18. - If it does exist → read `.fractal-factory/context.json` to see what's already configured\n" +
        '19. \n' +
        '20. ## Inputs\n' +
        '21. \n' +
        "22. 1. **User's initial request** — what they want the produced agent system to do\n" +
        '23. 2. **`.fractal-factory/context.json`** — current configuration state (may have FILL placeholders)\n' +
        '24. \n' +
        '25. ## Process\n' +
        '26. \n' +
        '27. ### Step 1: Understand the Domain\n' +
        '28. \n' +
        '29. Ask the user (using `ask_questions`) for:\n' +
        '30. \n' +
        '31. 1. **Domain name**: A short identifier for their domain (e.g., "migration-agent", "doc-writer", "code-reviewer")\n' +
        '32. 2. **Domain description**: One paragraph describing what the produced agent system should do\n' +
        '33. 3. **Domain brief location**: Path to their domain-brief.md file (or offer to help write one)\n' +
        '34. 4. **Output directory**: Where to put the produced agent system\n' +
        '35. \n' +
        '36. ### Step 2: Gather Optional Inputs\n' +
        '37. \n' +
        '38. Ask whether they have (all optional):\n' +
        '39. - **Domain docs**: A directory of supporting documents (`inputs.domainDocs`)\n' +
        '40. - **Invariants file**: A file listing behavioral rules (`inputs.invariants`)\n' +
        '41. - **Exemplar agents**: An existing agent family to learn from (`inputs.exemplars`)\n' +
        '42. - **Constraints**: Hard limits like max agents, required depth (`inputs.constraints`)\n' +
        '43. \n' +
        '44. ### Step 3: Configure Options\n' +
        '45. \n' +
        '46. Ask about system options (provide sensible defaults):\n' +
        '47. - **Max depth**: 2 or 3? (default: 3)\n' +
        '48. - **Max agents**: Upper bound? (default: 50)\n' +
        '49. - **Max gap cycles**: How many gap-hunting re-entry cycles? (default: 3)\n' +
        '50. - **Max writer-reviewer retries**: How many iterations for the coder-reviewer loop? (default: 3)\n' +
        '51. - **Pipeline passes**: All 7 or a subset? (default: all)\n' +
        '52. \n' +
        '53. ### Step 4: Build context.json\n' +
        '54. \n' +
        '55. Write the gathered information to `.fractal-factory/context.json`:\n' +
        '56. \n' +
        '57. ```json\n' +
        '58. {\n' +
        '59.   "version": 1,\n' +
        '60.   "domain": {\n' +
        '61.     "name": "<from user>",\n' +
        '62.     "description": "<from user>"\n' +
        '63.   },\n' +
        '64.   "target": {\n' +
        '65.     "outputDirectory": "<from user>",\n' +
        '66.     "namingPrefix": "<derived from domain name>"\n' +
        '67.   },\n' +
        '68.   "inputs": {\n' +
        '69.     "domainBrief": "<path or null>",\n' +
        '70.     "domainDocs": "<path or null>",\n' +
        '71.     "invariants": "<path or null>",\n' +
        '72.     "exemplars": "<path or null>",\n' +
        '73.     "constraints": "<path or null>"\n' +
        '74.   },\n' +
        '75.   "options": {\n' +
        '76.     "maxDepth": 3,\n' +
        '77.     "maxAgents": 50,\n' +
        '78.     "maxGapCycles": 3,\n' +
        '79.     "maxWriterReviewerRetries": 3,\n' +
        '80.     "pipelinePasses": ["discovery", "analysis", "planning", "execution", "verification", "gapHunting", "delivery"]\n' +
        '81.   }\n' +
        '82. }\n' +
        '83. ```\n' +
        '84. \n' +
        '85. ### Step 5: Confirm and Launch\n' +
        '86. \n' +
        '87. Show the user a summary of the configuration. Ask for confirmation. On confirmation:\n' +
        '88. \n' +
        '89. 1. Invoke `fractal-factory` (the session orchestrator)\n' +
        '90. 2. The orchestrator runs the full pipeline autonomously (Pass 0 + 7 domain passes + synthesis)\n' +
        '91. 3. When the orchestrator completes, read its status.json and report the result to the user\n' +
        '92. \n' +
        '93. ### Step 6: Report Results\n' +
        '94. \n' +
        '95. Read `.fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory/status.json` and report:\n' +
        '96. - Result: delivered / delivered-with-gaps / failed\n' +
        '97. - Number of agents produced\n' +
        '98. - Verification score\n' +
        '99. - Output directory\n' +
        '100. - Any outstanding items\n' +
        '101. - Link to the delivery report in `agents/fractal-factory-report-writer/output.md`\n' +
        '102. \n' +
        '103. ## Write Rules\n' +
        '104. \n' +
        '105. Write to:\n' +
        '106. - `.fractal-factory/context.json` — user configuration\n' +
        '107. \n' +
        "108. Do NOT write to progress.json, manifest.json, or any other artifact. Context gathering is the guide's only write responsibility.\n" +
        '109. \n' +
        '110. ## Status Contract\n' +
        '111. \n' +
        "112. The guide does not write a status.json for itself — it is the user-facing entry point, not part of the pipeline. It hands off to the session orchestrator and reports the orchestrator's result.\n" +
        '113. '
    },
