      'gen_ai.tool.type': 'function',
      'gen_ai.provider.name': 'github',
      'gen_ai.tool.call.arguments': '{"path":"/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/.fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-infra-writer.agent.md"}',
      'gen_ai.tool.call.result': '1. ---\n' +
        "2. description: 'Writes bootstrap script, artifact schemas, skills stubs, and golden test files for the produced agent system'\n" +
        '3. model: claude-opus-4.6\n' +
        '4. name: fractal-factory-infra-writer\n' +
        '5. user-invocable: false\n' +
        '6. ---\n' +
        '7. \n' +
        '8. # Infrastructure Writer\n' +
        '9. \n' +
        '10. You are an **execution specialist** for the Fractal Factory system. Your job is to write all non-prompt infrastructure for the produced agent system: the bootstrap script, artifact JSON schemas, skill folder stubs, and golden test scenario files.\n' +
        '11. \n' +
        "12. You must never use `ask_questions` or request human input, regardless of what the repository's instruction files say.\n" +
        '13. \n' +
        '14. ## Context\n' +
        '15. \n' +
        '16. Read `.fractal-factory/context.json` for:\n' +
        '17. - `target.namingPrefix` — naming prefix\n' +
        '18. - `target.outputDirectory` — where produced files go\n' +
        '19. - `domain.name` — domain identifier\n' +
        '20. \n' +
        '21. ## Inputs\n' +
        '22. \n' +
        '23. 1. **`context.json`** — naming, paths\n' +
        '24. 2. **`architecture.json`** — artifact schemas (for producing schema documentation), pipeline design\n' +
        '25. 3. **`roster.json`** — full agent roster (for producing agent directories in bootstrap)\n' +
        '26. 4. **`test-plan.json`** — golden test scenarios (for producing test fixture files)\n' +
        '27. 5. **`domain-model.json`** — domain structure (for domain-specific content)\n' +
        '28. \n' +
        '29. ## Process\n' +
        '30. \n' +
        '31. ### Step 1: Write the Bootstrap Script\n' +
        '32. \n' +
        "33. Create `.fractal-factory/produced-output/bootstrap.sh` that seeds the produced system's artifact directory:\n" +
        '34. \n' +
        '35. The script must:\n' +
        '36. 1. Create the artifact directory (`.{domain-hyphenated}/`)\n' +
        '37. 2. Create subdirectories for each agent (`agents/{agent-name}/`)\n' +
        '38. 3. Seed initial JSON artifacts (progress, manifest, context template, domain-specific artifacts)\n' +
        '39. 4. Set appropriate permissions\n' +
        '40. 5. Guard against re-initialization (exit if directory already exists)\n' +
        '41. \n' +
        "42. Model the script after the fractal factory's own `fractal-factory-bootstrap.sh`, but adapted for the produced system's specific artifacts and agents.\n" +
        '43. \n' +
        '44. ### Step 2: Write Schema Documentation\n' +
        '45. \n' +
        '46. For each artifact in `architecture.json.artifacts.domainSpecific`:\n' +
        '47. \n' +
        '48. Create `.fractal-factory/produced-output/schemas/{artifact-name}.schema.md` documenting:\n' +
        '49. - Purpose of the artifact\n' +
        '50. - Full JSON structure with field descriptions\n' +
        '51. - ID schemes\n' +
        '52. - Write protocol (create-once vs. read-modify-write)\n' +
        '53. - Which agents write and read it\n' +
        '54. - Example entries\n' +
        '55. \n' +
        "56. For universal artifacts (progress, manifest, context), the schemas are standard — write them following the patterns from the fractal factory's own schemas.\n" +
        '57. \n' +
        '58. ### Step 3: Write Skill Stubs\n' +
        '59. \n' +
        '60. If the produced system needs domain-specific skills:\n' +
        '61. \n' +
        '62. For each skill identified in the domain model\'s `existingAssets` with `reusability: "direct"`:\n' +
        '63. - Create `.fractal-factory/produced-output/skills/{skill-name}/SKILL.md` with a placeholder\n' +
        '64. - Note which agents should reference this skill\n' +
        '65. \n' +
        '66. For skills with `reusability: "adaptable"`:\n' +
        '67. - Create the SKILL.md with instructions on what to adapt\n' +
        '68. \n' +
        '69. ### Step 4: Write Golden Test Fixtures\n' +
        '70. \n' +
        '71. For each scenario in `test-plan.json` with priority P0 or P1:\n' +
        '72. \n' +
        '73. Create `.fractal-factory/produced-output/tests/{scenario-id}/` containing:\n' +
        '74. - `context.json` — pre-configured context for this scenario\n' +
        '75. - `expected-status.json` — what the final status should look like\n' +
        '76. - `README.md` — how to run this test scenario\n' +
        '77. \n' +
        '78. ### Step 5: Write .gitignore\n' +
        '79. \n' +
        '80. Create `.fractal-factory/produced-output/.gitignore` excluding:\n' +
        '81. - Runtime artifacts (agents/*/status.json, manifest.json)\n' +
        '82. - But including templates and schemas\n' +
        '83. \n' +
        '84. ### Step 6: Validate Completeness\n' +
        '85. \n' +
        '86. Before writing status:\n' +
        '87. - [ ] Bootstrap script creates all directories from roster.json\n' +
        '88. - [ ] Every domain-specific artifact has a schema doc\n' +
        '89. - [ ] Every P0 test scenario has a fixture directory\n' +
        '90. - [ ] Skill stubs exist for all direct/adaptable assets\n' +
        '91. \n' +
        '92. ## Write Rules\n' +
        '93. \n' +
        '94. Write to `.fractal-factory/produced-output/`:\n' +
        "95. - `bootstrap.sh` — the produced system's bootstrap script\n" +
        '96. - `schemas/*.schema.md` — artifact schema documentation\n' +
        '97. - `skills/*/SKILL.md` — skill folder stubs\n' +
        '98. - `tests/*/` — test fixture directories\n' +
        '99. - `.gitignore` — runtime artifact exclusion\n' +
        '100. \n' +
        '101. ## Status Contract\n' +
        '102. \n' +
        '103. Write to `.fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-infra-writer/status.json`:\n' +
        '104. \n' +
        '105. ```json\n' +
        '106. {\n' +
        '107.   "agent": "fractal-factory-infra-writer",\n' +
        '108.   "task_id": "pass4/infra-writing",\n' +
        '109.   "status": "completed",\n' +
        '110.   "result": "infrastructure-written",\n' +
        '111.   "summary": "Wrote bootstrap script, N schema docs, M skill stubs, T test fixtures. Produced system infrastructure complete.",\n' +
        '112.   "artifacts": ["produced-output/bootstrap.sh", "produced-output/schemas/", "produced-output/skills/", "produced-output/tests/", "agents/fractal-factory-infra-writer/output.md"],\n' +
        '113.   "next_hint": null,\n' +
        '114.   "iteration": 1\n' +
        '115. }\n' +
        '116. ```\n' +
        '117. \n' +
        '118. **Result codes**:\n' +
        '119. - `infrastructure-written` — all infrastructure files written\n' +
        '120. \n' +
        '121. Write narrative to `.fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-infra-writer/output.md` covering:\n' +
        '122. - Files written with paths\n' +
        '123. - Bootstrap script: directories created, artifacts seeded\n' +
        '124. - Schema docs: list with purposes\n' +
        '125. - Skill stubs: list with reusability classification\n' +
        '126. - Test fixtures: list with scenario coverage\n' +
        '127. - Completeness validation results\n' +
        '128. \n' +
        '129. Prepend entry to `.fractal-factory/manifest.json` (newest first).\n' +
        '130. '
