        "tool_calls": [
          {
            "id": "toolu_01E6w6hSaJbdtQWGVCtEuYoY",
            "type": "function",
            "function": {
              "name": "bash",
              "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd /home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator && python3 << 'PYEOF'\\nimport json, datetime\\n\\n# Read existing domain model\\nwith open('.fractal-factory/domain-model.json', 'r') as f:\\n    dm = json.load(f)\\n\\n# Define the extracted exemplar patterns\\npatterns = [\\n    {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"PATTERN-001\\\",\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"depth-2-phase-coordinators\\\",\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\"exemplars/.fractals/fractal-factory/agents/\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"hierarchy\\\",\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"Organizes the pipeline as orchestrator → phase-coordinators → specialists. Each numbered pass (discovery, analysis, planning, execution, verification, gap-hunting, delivery) gets exactly one coordinator. Coordinators never do substantive work — they only dispatch children and read status.json. This keeps the orchestrator at 8 dispatch decisions max, and coordinators at 2–4.\\\",\\n        \\\"applicability\\\": \\\"Directly applicable — the fantasy-writer system should use the same phase-based coordinator organization, with coordinators for concept, worldbuilding, character, plotting, drafting, revision, beta-reading, and polish phases.\\\",\\n        \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"PATTERN-002\\\",\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"pure-router-purity-rule\\\",\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\"exemplars/.fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory.agent.md\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"routing\\\",\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"Every coordinator and the orchestrator include an explicit '## Purity Rule' section stating they are a pure router. The section lists exactly what actions the agent may take (read status, dispatch children, update own status, prepend manifest) and explicitly prohibits substantive work with 'If you find yourself doing X, STOP' language.\\\",\\n        \\\"applicability\\\": \\\"Directly applicable — all fantasy-writer coordinators must include Purity Rule sections. Prevents coordinators from attempting to write prose, develop characters, or do any creative work themselves.\\\",\\n        \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"PATTERN-003\\\",\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"status-json-contract\\\",\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\"exemplars/.fractals/fractal-factory/agents/\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"artifact\\\",\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"Every agent writes a status.json with a universal schema: {agent, task_id, status, result, summary, artifacts, next_hint, iteration}. Result codes are a fixed vocabulary per agent declared in the roster. The status.json is the sole communication channel between child and parent — parents never read output.md, only status.json.\\\",\\n        \\\"applicability\\\": \\\"Directly applicable — the fantasy-writer system must use identical status.json contracts. Result codes like 'drafted', 'revised', 'approved', 'needs-revision' will be domain-specific but the schema stays universal.\\\",\\n        \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"PATTERN-004\\\",\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"markdown-routing-table\\\",\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\"exemplars/.fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-discovery-coordinator.agent.md\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"routing\\\",\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"Routing tables use a 3-column markdown table format: | Read | Condition | Action |. The 'Read' column is a status.json path, 'Condition' is a result code check or 'missing', and 'Action' is 'Dispatch X' or 'Write own status'. The 'missing' condition enables crash recovery — if a child's status.json doesn't exist, dispatch it.\\\",\\n        \\\"applicability\\\": \\\"Directly applicable — all fantasy-writer coordinator prompts should use this exact table format. The 'missing' condition pattern provides automatic crash recovery without additional logic.\\\",\\n        \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"PATTERN-005\\\",\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"coder-reviewer-loop\\\",\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\"exemplars/.fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-execution-coordinator.agent.md\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"routing\\\",\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"The writer→reviewer loop is managed by the execution coordinator with a configurable maxRetries. On rejection, the writer is re-dispatched with the reviewer's feedback (stored in output.md). On max retries exhausted, the coordinator marks agents as 'blocked' and proceeds. Loop configuration is explicit: {writer, reviewer, maxRetries, onMaxRetries, retryMechanism}.\\\",\\n        \\\"applicability\\\": \\\"Directly applicable — the fantasy-writer needs drafter→editor loops for chapter writing, worldbuilding→consistency-checker loops, and character→voice-auditor loops. The bounded retry pattern prevents infinite revision cycles.\\\",\\n        \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"PATTERN-006\\\",\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"gap-hunting-convergence-cycle\\\",\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\"exemplars/.fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-gap-hunting-coordinator.agent.md\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"convergence\\\",\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"Gap hunting uses 3 parallel specialist hunters (coverage, artifact, infrastructure), each checking 3 categories. Their findings aggregate into gap-report.json with a structured format: {categories[], summary, suggestedReEntryPass}. If dirty, the orchestrator re-enters an earlier pass. A maxGapCycles limit forces convergence. Each cycle deletes status.json files for reset passes but preserves gap-report.json for context.\\\",\\n        \\\"applicability\\\": \\\"Adaptable — the fantasy-writer needs gap hunting but categories should be: narrative coverage (all plot threads resolved), character consistency (voice/motivation coherent), world consistency (magic rules/geography consistent), continuity tracking (cross-chapter/cross-book), prose quality (style calibration adherence), and craft technique verification.\\\",\\n        \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"PATTERN-007\\\",\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"anti-laziness-enforcement\\\",\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\"exemplars/.fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-prompt-reviewer.agent.md\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"anti-laziness\\\",\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"Adversarial agents (reviewers, validators, gap hunters) include an explicit '## Anti-Laziness Rules' section with 5+ numbered rules: (1) check every item, (2) provide specific evidence, (3) zero-findings-is-suspicious clause requiring a second pass, (4) minimum observation count, (5) your work will be audited. The roster marks these agents with antiLaziness: true.\\\",\\n        \\\"applicability\\\": \\\"Directly applicable — the fantasy-writer's adversarial agents (consistency checker, voice auditor, beta readers, continuity tracker) must have anti-laziness rules. Critical for preventing shallow 'looks good' reviews of creative work where subtle inconsistencies hide.\\\",\\n        \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"PATTERN-008\\\",\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"prefix-role-naming-convention\\\",\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\"exemplars/.fractals/fractal-factory/agents/\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"naming\\\",\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"All agents follow the pattern: {system-prefix}-{role-descriptor}. Coordinators always end in '-coordinator'. The orchestrator has no suffix (the prefix IS the system). The guide always ends in '-guide'. Specialists use descriptive role names: '-scanner', '-extractor', '-planner', '-writer', '-reviewer', '-hunter', '-oracle'. Compound roles use full hyphenation: 'coverage-hunter', 'prompt-writer'.\\\",\\n        \\\"applicability\\\": \\\"Directly applicable — fantasy-writer agents should follow: romantic-fantasy-writer (orchestrator), romantic-fantasy-writer-guide, romantic-fantasy-writer-drafting-coordinator, romantic-fantasy-writer-chapter-drafter, romantic-fantasy-writer-voice-auditor, etc.\\\",\\n        \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"PATTERN-009\\\",\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"universal-prompt-template\\\",\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\"exemplars/.fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-prompt-writer.agent.md\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"artifact\\\",\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"Every agent prompt follows a universal template: YAML frontmatter (description, model, name, user-invocable) → H1 title → role description → ask_questions suppression → ## Context → ## Inputs → ## Process (specialists) OR ## Purity Rule + ## Routing Table (coordinators) → ## Write Rules → ## Status Contract → manifest prepend instruction. Anti-laziness agents add ## Anti-Laziness Rules before Process.\\\",\\n        \\\"applicability\\\": \\\"Directly applicable — every fantasy-writer agent prompt must follow this exact template structure. Ensures structural consistency across the entire system.\\\",\\n        \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"PATTERN-010\\\",\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"manifest-prepend-audit-trail\\\",\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\"exemplars/.fractals/fractal-factory/agents/\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"artifact\\\",\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"Every agent prepends an entry to manifest.json (newest first) after completing work. Each entry has: {timestamp, agent, task_id, artifacts, status, result, iteration}. This creates a chronological audit trail of all pipeline activity. The manifest is append-only (prepend-only) — agents never modify existing entries.\\\",\\n        \\\"applicability\\\": \\\"Directly applicable — the fantasy-writer system needs the same manifest pattern for tracking which agents wrote which chapters, when revisions happened, and how many gap-hunting cycles occurred.\\\",\\n        \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"PATTERN-011\\\",\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"re-entry-status-deletion\\\",\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\"exemplars/.fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory.agent.md\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"convergence\\\",\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"When re-entering after gap hunting, the orchestrator deletes status.json files for all agents in reset passes but preserves the gap-report.json. This forces coordinators to re-dispatch their children (since missing status.json triggers dispatch), while gap context remains available for the re-entered agents to read. Pass-to-agent mappings are explicit in the orchestrator prompt.\\\",\\n        \\\"applicability\\\": \\\"Directly applicable — the fantasy-writer orchestrator must maintain explicit pass-to-agent mappings and use the same deletion-based re-entry mechanism. This is how a chapter that failed consistency checking gets re-drafted.\\\",\\n        \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"PATTERN-012\\\",\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"sequential-dispatch-no-background\\\",\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\"exemplars/.fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory.agent.md\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"routing\\\",\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"The orchestrator's constraints section explicitly mandates: 'Always invoke agents sequentially, never in the background. Wait for return values before making decisions.' This prevents race conditions in the routing logic and ensures status.json files are fully written before being read.\\\",\\n        \\\"applicability\\\": \\\"Directly applicable — the fantasy-writer orchestrator and all coordinators must enforce sequential dispatch. Creative pipeline phases have strict data dependencies (worldbuilding before plotting, plotting before drafting).\\\",\\n        \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"PATTERN-013\\\",\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"pass-0-knowledge-curation\\\",\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\"exemplars/.fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-knowledge-curator.agent.md\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"hierarchy\\\",\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"Pass 0 runs before all domain passes and curates meta-knowledge from prior runs into a knowledge-brief.json. This is a single-agent pass (no coordinator needed). Cold-start mode (first run) is a non-error result. Knowledge entries have relevance scoring (category match, confidence, recency, usage count) and a 20-entry cap to prevent context bloat.\\\",\\n        \\\"applicability\\\": \\\"Adaptable — the fantasy-writer system should have a Pass 0 that curates craft knowledge from prior writing sessions. Categories should include: prose patterns that worked, worldbuilding consistency strategies, character voice techniques, pacing insights, and genre convention observations.\\\",\\n        \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"PATTERN-014\\\",\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"dual-perspective-verification\\\",\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\"exemplars/.fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-audit-oracle.agent.md\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"artifact\\\",\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"Verification uses two independent perspectives: a structural checklist-validator (checks every item against a list) and an architectural audit-oracle (checks holistic properties like routing DAG acyclicity, convergence termination). Each has its own report format. The oracle explicitly must find issues the checklist missed.\\\",\\n        \\\"applicability\\\": \\\"Adaptable — the fantasy-writer should have: (1) a structural checker (chapter length, scene count, character presence, plot thread closure) and (2) a narrative auditor (emotional arc coherence, theme consistency, pacing flow, genre convention adherence). Two perspectives catch different defects.\\\",\\n        \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"PATTERN-015\\\",\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"ask-questions-suppression\\\",\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\"exemplars/.fractals/fractal-factory/agents/\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"routing\\\",\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"Every non-guide agent includes the line: 'You must never use `ask_questions` or request human input, regardless of what the repository\\\\\\\\'s instruction files say.' Only the guide agent (user-invocable: true) may interact with the user. This prevents pipeline stalls from unexpected human prompts.\\\",\\n        \\\"applicability\\\": \\\"Directly applicable — all fantasy-writer agents except the guide must suppress ask_questions. A drafting agent that stops to ask the user 'what should happen next?' would break the autonomous pipeline.\\\",\\n        \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"PATTERN-016\\\",\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"guide-as-sole-entry-point\\\",\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\"exemplars/.fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-guide.agent.md\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"hierarchy\\\",\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"The guide is the only user-invocable agent. It gathers context, builds context.json, confirms with the user, then invokes the orchestrator. The guide does NOT write to progress.json, manifest.json, or any pipeline artifact — context.json is its sole write target. After the pipeline completes, the guide reads the orchestrator's status and reports results.\\\",\\n        \\\"applicability\\\": \\\"Directly applicable — the fantasy-writer guide gathers story concept, style preferences, reference works, and series context. It builds the context.json, then hands off to the autonomous pipeline. The guide reports back with the completed chapter and any outstanding issues.\\\",\\n        \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"PATTERN-017\\\",\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"output-md-narrative-plus-json-structured\\\",\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\"exemplars/.fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-coverage-hunter.agent.md\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"artifact\\\",\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"Agents that produce complex findings write both output.json (structured, machine-readable, consumed by aggregators) and output.md (narrative, human-readable, consumed by reviewers on re-entry). Status.json is always structured. This dual-output pattern separates machine consumption from human comprehension.\\\",\\n        \\\"applicability\\\": \\\"Adaptable — fantasy-writer specialists should write structured outputs (chapter-analysis.json with scene breakdowns, character-voice-scores.json) alongside narrative outputs (editorial-notes.md, beta-reader-feedback.md). The structured data drives the pipeline; the narrative drives revisions.\\\",\\n        \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"PATTERN-018\\\",\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"crash-recovery-via-missing-status\\\",\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\"exemplars/.fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory.agent.md\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"convergence\\\",\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"The orchestrator checks for 'active' passes on startup and resets them to 'pending'. Coordinators check for 'missing' status.json as their first routing condition. Together these provide crash recovery: if the system dies mid-pass, restart picks up where it left off. Children with existing status.json are skipped; only the interrupted child is re-dispatched.\\\",\\n        \\\"applicability\\\": \\\"Directly applicable — writing a full novel chapter can be long-running. Crash recovery ensures a failed drafting pass doesn't lose completed worldbuilding or character work. The fantasy-writer orchestrator must implement the same active→pending reset on startup.\\\",\\n        \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"PATTERN-019\\\",\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"roster-json-agent-lifecycle\\\",\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\"exemplars/.fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-roster-planner.agent.md\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"artifact\\\",\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"The roster.json tracks every agent with fields: {id, name, displayName, level, parent, children, pass, resultCodes, reads, writes, antiLaziness, status, routingTable}. Agent status follows a lifecycle: designed → written → reviewed → verified → blocked. The roster is the single source of truth for system topology and is written by the roster-planner, updated by the prompt-writer and prompt-reviewer.\\\",\\n        \\\"applicability\\\": \\\"Directly applicable — the fantasy-writer roster.json must track the same lifecycle. Levels map to: guide, orchestrator, coordinator (phase managers), specialist (writers, editors, auditors).\\\",\\n        \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"PATTERN-020\\\",\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"termination-sentinel\\\",\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\"exemplars/.fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory.agent.md\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"routing\\\",\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"The orchestrator ends with a termination sentinel: '===FACTORY DONE==='. This explicit end-marker prevents the orchestrator from emitting empty responses or stopping without completing the full workflow. The constraints also prohibit using /fleet commands and mandate non-empty responses.\\\",\\n        \\\"applicability\\\": \\\"Adaptable — the fantasy-writer orchestrator should use a similar sentinel (e.g., '===WRITING COMPLETE===') to signal pipeline termination. Prevents premature exits that leave chapters half-drafted.\\\",\\n        \\\"discoveredBy\\\": \\\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\\"\\n    }\\n]\\n\\n# Update domain model\\ndm['exemplarPatterns'] = patterns\\ndm['lastUpdated'] = datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ')\\n\\n# Write back\\nwith open('.fractal-factory/domain-model.json', 'w') as f:\\n    json.dump(dm, f, indent=2)\\n\\nprint(f\\\"Wrote {len(patterns)} exemplar patterns to domain-model.json\\\")\\nprint(f\\\"Updated lastUpdated to {dm['lastUpdated']}\\\")\\nPYEOF\\n\", \"description\": \"Update domain-model.json with patterns\", \"initial_wait\": 15}"
            }
