      'gen_ai.tool.call.arguments': `{"command":"cd /home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator && python3 << 'PYEOF'\\nimport json, datetime\\n\\n# Read existing domain model\\nwith open('.fractal-factory/domain-model.json', 'r') as f:\\n    dm = json.load(f)\\n\\n# Define the extracted exemplar patterns\\npatterns = [\\n    {\\n        \\"id\\": \\"PATTERN-001\\",\\n        \\"name\\": \\"depth-2-phase-coordinators\\",\\n        \\"source\\": \\"exemplars/.fractals/fractal-factory/agents/\\",\\n        \\"category\\": \\"hierarchy\\",\\n        \\"description\\": \\"Organizes the pipeline as orchestrator → phase-coordinators → specialists. Each numbered pass (discovery, analysis, planning, execution, verification, gap-hunting, delivery) gets exactly one coordinator. Coordinators never do substantive work — they only dispatch children and read status.json. This keeps the orchestrator at 8 dispatch decisions max, and coordinators at 2–4.\\",\\n        \\"applicability\\": \\"Directly applicable — the fantasy-writer system should use the same phase-based coordinator organization, with coordinators for concept, worldbuilding, character, plotting, drafting, revision, beta-reading, and polish phases.\\",\\n        \\"discoveredBy\\": \\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\"id\\": \\"PATTERN-002\\",\\n        \\"name\\": \\"pure-router-purity-rule\\",\\n        \\"source\\": \\"exemplars/.fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory.agent.md\\",\\n        \\"category\\": \\"routing\\",\\n        \\"description\\": \\"Every coordinator and the orchestrator include an explicit '## Purity Rule' section stating they are a pure router. The section lists exactly what actions the agent may take (read status, dispatch children, update own status, prepend manifest) and explicitly prohibits substantive work with 'If you find yourself doing X, STOP' language.\\",\\n        \\"applicability\\": \\"Directly applicable — all fantasy-writer coordinators must include Purity Rule sections. Prevents coordinators from attempting to write prose, develop characters, or do any creative work themselves.\\",\\n        \\"discoveredBy\\": \\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\"id\\": \\"PATTERN-003\\",\\n        \\"name\\": \\"status-json-contract\\",\\n        \\"source\\": \\"exemplars/.fractals/fractal-factory/agents/\\",\\n        \\"category\\": \\"artifact\\",\\n        \\"description\\": \\"Every agent writes a status.json with a universal schema: {agent, task_id, status, result, summary, artifacts, next_hint, iteration}. Result codes are a fixed vocabulary per agent declared in the roster. The status.json is the sole communication channel between child and parent — parents never read output.md, only status.json.\\",\\n        \\"applicability\\": \\"Directly applicable — the fantasy-writer system must use identical status.json contracts. Result codes like 'drafted', 'revised', 'approved', 'needs-revision' will be domain-specific but the schema stays universal.\\",\\n        \\"discoveredBy\\": \\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\"id\\": \\"PATTERN-004\\",\\n        \\"name\\": \\"markdown-routing-table\\",\\n        \\"source\\": \\"exemplars/.fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-discovery-coordinator.agent.md\\",\\n        \\"category\\": \\"routing\\",\\n        \\"description\\": \\"Routing tables use a 3-column markdown table format: | Read | Condition | Action |. The 'Read' column is a status.json path, 'Condition' is a result code check or 'missing', and 'Action' is 'Dispatch X' or 'Write own status'. The 'missing' condition enables crash recovery — if a child's status.json doesn't exist, dispatch it.\\",\\n        \\"applicability\\": \\"Directly applicable — all fantasy-writer coordinator prompts should use this exact table format. The 'missing' condition pattern provides automatic crash recovery without additional logic.\\",\\n        \\"discoveredBy\\": \\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\"id\\": \\"PATTERN-005\\",\\n        \\"name\\": \\"coder-reviewer-loop\\",\\n        \\"source\\": \\"exemplars/.fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-execution-coordinator.agent.md\\",\\n        \\"category\\": \\"routing\\",\\n        \\"description\\": \\"The writer→reviewer loop is managed by the execution coordinator with a configurable maxRetries. On rejection, the writer is re-dispatched with the reviewer's feedback (stored in output.md). On max retries exhausted, the coordinator marks agents as 'blocked' and proceeds. Loop configuration is explicit: {writer, reviewer, maxRetries, onMaxRetries, retryMechanism}.\\",\\n        \\"applicability\\": \\"Directly applicable — the fantasy-writer needs drafter→editor loops for chapter writing, worldbuilding→consistency-checker loops, and character→voice-auditor loops. The bounded retry pattern prevents infinite revision cycles.\\",\\n        \\"discoveredBy\\": \\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\"id\\": \\"PATTERN-006\\",\\n        \\"name\\": \\"gap-hunting-convergence-cycle\\",\\n        \\"source\\": \\"exemplars/.fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-gap-hunting-coordinator.agent.md\\",\\n        \\"category\\": \\"convergence\\",\\n        \\"description\\": \\"Gap hunting uses 3 parallel specialist hunters (coverage, artifact, infrastructure), each checking 3 categories. Their findings aggregate into gap-report.json with a structured format: {categories[], summary, suggestedReEntryPass}. If dirty, the orchestrator re-enters an earlier pass. A maxGapCycles limit forces convergence. Each cycle deletes status.json files for reset passes but preserves gap-report.json for context.\\",\\n        \\"applicability\\": \\"Adaptable — the fantasy-writer needs gap hunting but categories should be: narrative coverage (all plot threads resolved), character consistency (voice/motivation coherent), world consistency (magic rules/geography consistent), continuity tracking (cross-chapter/cross-book), prose quality (style calibration adherence), and craft technique verification.\\",\\n        \\"discoveredBy\\": \\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\"id\\": \\"PATTERN-007\\",\\n        \\"name\\": \\"anti-laziness-enforcement\\",\\n        \\"source\\": \\"exemplars/.fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-prompt-reviewer.agent.md\\",\\n        \\"category\\": \\"anti-laziness\\",\\n        \\"description\\": \\"Adversarial agents (reviewers, validators, gap hunters) include an explicit '## Anti-Laziness Rules' section with 5+ numbered rules: (1) check every item, (2) provide specific evidence, (3) zero-findings-is-suspicious clause requiring a second pass, (4) minimum observation count, (5) your work will be audited. The roster marks these agents with antiLaziness: true.\\",\\n        \\"applicability\\": \\"Directly applicable — the fantasy-writer's adversarial agents (consistency checker, voice auditor, beta readers, continuity tracker) must have anti-laziness rules. Critical for preventing shallow 'looks good' reviews of creative work where subtle inconsistencies hide.\\",\\n        \\"discoveredBy\\": \\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\"id\\": \\"PATTERN-008\\",\\n        \\"name\\": \\"prefix-role-naming-convention\\",\\n        \\"source\\": \\"exemplars/.fractals/fractal-factory/agents/\\",\\n        \\"category\\": \\"naming\\",\\n        \\"description\\": \\"All agents follow the pattern: {system-prefix}-{role-descriptor}. Coordinators always end in '-coordinator'. The orchestrator has no suffix (the prefix IS the system). The guide always ends in '-guide'. Specialists use descriptive role names: '-scanner', '-extractor', '-planner', '-writer', '-reviewer', '-hunter', '-oracle'. Compound roles use full hyphenation: 'coverage-hunter', 'prompt-writer'.\\",\\n        \\"applicability\\": \\"Directly applicable — fantasy-writer agents should follow: romantic-fantasy-writer (orchestrator), romantic-fantasy-writer-guide, romantic-fantasy-writer-drafting-coordinator, romantic-fantasy-writer-chapter-drafter, romantic-fantasy-writer-voice-auditor, etc.\\",\\n        \\"discoveredBy\\": \\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\"id\\": \\"PATTERN-009\\",\\n        \\"name\\": \\"universal-prompt-template\\",\\n        \\"source\\": \\"exemplars/.fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-prompt-writer.agent.md\\",\\n        \\"category\\": \\"artifact\\",\\n        \\"description\\": \\"Every agent prompt follows a universal template: YAML frontmatter (description, model, name, user-invocable) → H1 title → role description → ask_questions suppression → ## Context → ## Inputs → ## Process (specialists) OR ## Purity Rule + ## Routing Table (coordinators) → ## Write Rules → ## Status Contract → manifest prepend instruction. Anti-laziness agents add ## Anti-Laziness Rules before Process.\\",\\n        \\"applicability\\": \\"Directly applicable — every fantasy-writer agent prompt must follow this exact template structure. Ensures structural consistency across the entire system.\\",\\n        \\"discoveredBy\\": \\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\"id\\": \\"PATTERN-010\\",\\n        \\"name\\": \\"manifest-prepend-audit-trail\\",\\n        \\"source\\": \\"exemplars/.fractals/fractal-factory/agents/\\",\\n        \\"category\\": \\"artifact\\",\\n        \\"description\\": \\"Every agent prepends an entry to manifest.json (newest first) after completing work. Each entry has: {timestamp, agent, task_id, artifacts, status, result, iteration}. This creates a chronological audit trail of all pipeline activity. The manifest is append-only (prepend-only) — agents never modify existing entries.\\",\\n        \\"applicability\\": \\"Directly applicable — the fantasy-writer system needs the same manifest pattern for tracking which agents wrote which chapters, when revisions happened, and how many gap-hunting cycles occurred.\\",\\n        \\"discoveredBy\\": \\"fractal-factory-exemplar-analyzer\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n        \\"id\\": \\"PATTERN-011\\",\\n        \\"name\\": \\"re-entry-status-deletion\\",\\n        \\"source\\": \\"exemplars/.fractals/fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory.agent.md\\",\\n `... 9786 more characters,
