rpose, coordinator, specialist agents, and parallelization potential. Discovery scans the domain and is already complete with four specialists. Analysis determines the architecture and artifact schemas with three independent analysis agents. I'm continuing through the remaining passes...\n\nPass 3 focuses on planning the agent roster and routing tables, which requires sequential work since routing depends on the roster decisions. Pass 4 handles writing all the prompts and infrastructure with a writer-reviewer loop that can retry up to ten times. Pass 5 validates everything against the invariants and architecture we've established.\n\nFor verification, I'm running two independent validators in parallel—one checking against a checklist and another providing an audit perspective. Pass 6 hunts for gaps across three independent dimensions: coverage, artifacts, and infrastructure. Finally, Pass 7 packages everything up with documentation and reporting, completing the delivery phase.\n\nThe re-entry logic handles different scenarios: if gap hunting uncovers items needing fresh analysis, I loop back to Pass 2; if they're ready for planning, I jump to Pass 3; if they just need execution, I start at Pass 4. Verification failures send me back to Pass 4 to fix the issues. With 10 gap cycles allowed and the complexity of 14 subdomains with 81 invariants, there's room to catch and address problems iteratively.\n\nConvergence happens when gap hunting stops finding new items across all categories, at which point I move to delivery and flag any remaining outstanding items in the report. Now I'm working through the architecture.json pipeline section, status.json, output.md, and manifest.json to document this design.\n\nI need to be more precise about agent counts—the factory pipeline passes describe how the factory itself builds the system, not the agents in the produced system. The produced system has 14 subdomains, 10 creative phases plus 4 cross-cutting concerns, 81 invariants, with a max of 80 agents and depth 3. Let me refine the design with this distinction in mind.\n\nThe factory pipeline follows a consistent 7-pass structure, and what I'm customizing for this domain is which passes to include, the entry and exit conditions, re-entry rules based on complexity, agent estimates per pass, whether passes can run in parallel, and domain-specific notes about what each pass handles.",
