        '27.         "parallelizable": true,\n' +
        '28.         "notes": "Four specialists scan independent aspects: (1) domain-scanner extracts 14 subdomains from domain-brief.md, (2) invariant-extractor classifies 81 invariants into behavioral/quality/workflow/structural, (3) asset-auditor catalogs 26 reusable assets (7 shared-includes, 11 skills, 3 agent-templates, 4 tools, 1 MCP server), (4) exemplar-analyzer extracts 20 patterns from the fractal-factory exemplar family. All run in parallel under the coordinator. ALREADY COMPLETED in this run."\n' +
        '29.       },\n' +
        '30.       {\n' +
        '31.         "pass": 2,\n' +
        '32.         "name": "analysis",\n' +
        '33.         "displayName": "Architecture Analysis",\n' +
        '34.         "purpose": "Analyze the discovered domain model to determine three architectural decisions: (1) pipeline pass structure and re-entry rules for the produced fantasy-writer system, (2) shared artifact schemas and data flow contracts between agents, (3) hierarchy depth (depth-2 vs depth-3) per coordinator based on subdomain complexity. These three analyses are independent and inform the planning pass.",\n' +
        '35.         "entryCondition": "Pass 1 complete — domain-model.json exists with all four sections populated. Discovery coordinator status=completed.",\n' +
        '36.         "exitCondition": "All three analysis specialists (pipeline-architect, artifact-designer, depth-analyzer) report status=completed. architecture.json contains populated pipeline, artifacts, and depth sections.",\n' +
        '37.         "coordinatorHint": "fractal-factory-analysis-coordinator",\n' +
