        '52.         "notes": "Sequential dispatch required: roster-planner runs first (routing and tests depend on knowing agent names and hierarchy). Then routing-planner builds tables using the roster. Finally test-planner creates scenarios referencing both roster and routes. The 14-subdomain, 80-agent budget with depth-3 hierarchy makes this the most complex planning pass. Key decisions: how to allocate the agent budget across 10 sequential phases + 4 cross-cutting concerns, how many specialist writers vs. reviewers per creative phase, and how adversarial auditors integrate as sub-phase gates."\n' +
