        "content": "<overview>\nThe user asked me to act as the routing planner for the Fractal Factory pipeline, designing routing tables, re-entry rules, and convergence bounds for every coordinator and orchestrator in the **romantic-fantasy-writer** agent system — a 67-agent multi-level hierarchy for autonomous romantic fantasy fiction production. My approach was to read all input artifacts (roster.json, architecture.json, context.json), analyze the agent hierarchy and data dependencies, design routing tables for all 20 routing agents (1 orchestrator + 9 coordinators + 10 sub-coordinators), validate completeness, and write the results to `.fractal-factory/routing.json`.\n</overview>\n\n<history>\n1. The user provided detailed instructions to design routing tables for the romantic-fantasy-writer agent system\n   - Read `.fractal-factory/context.json` — confirmed maxGapCycles: 10, maxWriterReviewerRetries: 10, maxDepth: 3, maxAgents: 80\n   - Read `.fractal-factory/roster.json` — 67 agents: 1 guide, 1 orchestrator, 9 coordinators, 10 sub-coordinators, 46 specialists\n   - Read `.fractal-factory/architecture.json` — 8-pass pipeline, 42+ artifacts, 5 depth-3 coordinators, 4 depth-2 coordinators, 4 re-entry rules\n   - Analyzed agent hierarchy, data flow dependencies, and routing patterns needed for each coordinator type\n   - Built a comprehensive Python script to generate the routing.json with all 20 routing agent tables\n   - Generated routing.json (1456 lines, 161 routing entries) covering all agents\n   - Ran validation: confirmed all 20 routing agents covered, all block propagation paths valid, all loops bounded\n   - Discovered `revision-loop` transient state wasn't handled at orchestrator level — patched routing.json to add handling\n   - Created output.md narrative document with human-readable routing tables\n   - **Have NOT yet written**: status.json, manifest.json update\n</history>\n\n<work_done>\nFiles created:\n- `.fractal-factory/routing.json` — Complete routing tables for all 20 routing agents (161 entries)\n- `.fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-routing-planner/output.md` — Human-readable narrative of all routing decisions\n\nFiles NOT yet created (still pending):\n- `.fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-routing-planner/status.json` — Required status contract\n- `.fractal-factory/manifest.json` — Needs prepended entry (file already exists)\n\nWork completed:\n- [x] Read all input artifacts (context.json, roster.json, architecture.json)\n- [x] Designed orchestrator routing table (12-step phase sequence with revision↔beta loop)\n- [x] Designed 9 coordinator routing tables (8 with auditor gate loops, 1 without)\n- [x] Designed 10 sub-coordinator routing tables (7 sequential, 1 sequential per-chapter, 2 parallel)\n- [x] Validated routing completeness (20/20 agents, all result codes mapped, all blocks propagate)\n- [x] Fixed revision-loop transient state handling at orchestrator level\n- [x] Wrote output.md narrative\n- [ ] Write status.json for routing planner\n- [ ] Prepend manifest.json entry\n</work_done>\n\n<technical_details>\n**Agent Hierarchy Structure:**\n- Orchestrator routes 9 coordinators + 3 cross-cutting specialists (continuity-tracker, series-kb-manager, craft-tracker)\n- 5 depth-3 coordinators: worldbuilding, character, plotting, drafting, beta-reading (each has sub-coordinators)\n- 4 depth-2 coordinators: concept, style, revision, polish (direct specialist children)\n- Cross-cutting agents dispatched at specific transition points by orchestrator\n\n**Routing Patterns Used:**\n1. **Sequential with auditor gate loop** — Used by 8 coordinators. Pattern: dispatch children sequentially → auditor gates → if failed, reset all descendant statuses and retry (max 3). Feedback artifact from audit-reports/{phase}/gate.json feeds retry attempts.\n2. **Per-chapter iteration** — Used by drafting, revision, beta-reading, polish coordinators. Each chapter processed independently with per-chapter retry budget.\n3. **Parallel fan-out** — Used by genre-lens-coordinator (2 parallel readers) and craft-lens-coordinator (3 parallel readers). Also beta-reading-coordinator fans out genre-lens + craft-lens in parallel.\n4. **Revision ↔ beta-reading loop** — Orchestrator-level bounded loop (max 2 cycles). Triggered when beta-synthesis verdicts contain 'revision-required'.\n\n**Key Design Decisions:**\n- **Auditor retry limit: 3** (not the global maxWriterReviewerRetries=10 from context.json, which applies to the factory's prompt writer→reviewer loop, not the produced system's auditor gates)\n- **Revision ↔ beta cycle limit: 2** at orchestrator level\n- **On retry, depth-3 coordinators reset ALL descendant statuses** (full cascade through sub-coordinators and their specialists)\n- **Revision coordinator optimization:** On auditor retry, only chapter-reviser re-runs; the 3 editor reports (developmental, line, copy) are preserved as independent assessments\n- **Per-chapter retry counters reset per chapter** — each chapter gets its own independent retry budget\n- **Polish coordinator has no auditor loop** — it's the terminal phase, failures just report blocked\n\n**Transient States:**\n- `revision-loop` is reported by coordinators while in their internal auditor retry loop. Orchestrator treats this as \"wait and re-check\" — it always resolves to 'complete' or 'blocked'.\n\n**Validation Results:**\n- All 20 routing agents covered\n- All child result codes mapped (including transient `revision-loop`)\n- All block/failure codes propagate upward through the hierarchy\n- All 8 auditor loops bounded at maxRetries=3\n- All 4 per-chapter loops have iteration sources defined\n- 3 parallel dispatch groups identified and documented\n</technical_details>\n\n<important_files>\n- `.fractal-factory/routing.json`\n   - **Primary deliverable** — contains routing tables for all 20 routing agents\n   - Created from scratch via Python generation script\n   - 1456 lines, valid JSON, 161 routing entries total\n   - Structure: `{ version, lastUpdated, globalBounds, agents: { [agentName]: { routingTable, loopConfig, perChapterLoop, ... } } }`\n\n- `.fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-routing-planner/output.md`\n   - Human-readable narrative of all routing decisions\n   - Created from scratch, ~12K characters\n   - Contains ASCII flow diagrams, markdown tables for each coordinator, convergence bounds summary, validation results\n\n- `.fractal-factory/roster.json`\n   - **Primary input** — 67-agent roster with hierarchy, result codes, artifact assignments\n   - Read-only (not modified by routing planner)\n   - Key data: agent.children, agent.resultCodes, agent.level, agent.pass\n\n- `.fractal-factory/architecture.json`\n   - **Input** — pipeline design, artifact schemas, depth analysis, re-entry rules\n   - Read-only\n   - Key data: pipeline.passes (8 passes), pipeline.reEntryRules (4 rules), depth.decisions (9 coordinators), artifacts (42+ types)\n\n- `.fractal-factory/context.json`\n   - **Input** — global configuration\n   - Key values: maxGapCycles=10, maxWriterReviewerRetries=10, maxDepth=3, maxAgents=80\n\n- `.fractal-factory/manifest.json`\n   - Needs prepended entry (not yet done)\n   - Already exists from prior pipeline passes\n</important_files>\n\n<next_steps>\nRemaining work:\n- Write `.fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-routing-planner/status.json` with result: \"planned\"\n- Prepend entry to `.fractal-factory/manifest.json` (newest first)\n\nStatus.json should contain:\n```json\n{\n  \"agent\": \"fractal-factory-routing-planner\",\n  \"task_id\": \"pass3/routing-design\",\n  \"status\": \"completed\",\n  \"result\": \"planned\",\n  \"summary\": \"Designed routing tables for 9 coordinators + 10 sub-coordinators + 1 orchestrator. Total routing entries: 161. 8 auditor gate loops. 4 per-chapter iteration loops. 3 parallel dispatch groups. All routing gaps resolved.\",\n  \"artifacts\": [\"routing.json\", \"agents/fractal-factory-routing-planner/output.md\"],\n  \"next_hint\": \"fractal-factory-test-planner\",\n  \"iteration\": 1\n}\n```\n\nManifest entry should reference the routing planner completion with artifacts list.\n\nImmediate next actions:\n1. Write status.json\n2. Read existing manifest.json, prepend new entry\n3. Task is then complete\n</next_steps>",
