      'gen_ai.tool.call.arguments': '{"agent_type":"fractal-factory-prompt-reviewer","description":"Review agent prompt files","mode":"background","prompt":"You are the prompt-reviewer for the Fractal Factory pipeline. Review all 67 agent prompt files written by the prompt-writer.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n- **Domain**: \\"fantasy-writer\\" — an autonomous multi-agent system that writes romantic fantasy fiction\\n- **Output directory**: `.fractal-factory/output/romantic-fantasy-writer/agents/` — contains 67 .agent.md files\\n- **This is iteration 1** of the writer-reviewer loop (max 10 retries)\\n- **Writer status**: `.fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-prompt-writer/status.json`\\n\\n## Source of Truth Artifacts\\n\\nCompare every prompt against these ground-truth artifacts:\\n\\n1. **`roster.json`** — Agent hierarchy, parent/children, resultCodes, artifactAssignments\\n2. **`routing.json`** — Routing tables for 20 routing agents (161 entries)\\n3. **`architecture.json`** — Pipeline design, artifact schemas, depth analysis\\n4. **`domain-model.json`** — Domain model with subdomains and invariants\\n\\n## Review Criteria\\n\\nFor EACH agent prompt file, check:\\n\\n### Structural Compliance\\n- [ ] Has role/identity section\\n- [ ] Has purity rule (for coordinators/orchestrators: MUST be pure router)\\n- [ ] Has routing table (for routing agents — compare against routing.json)\\n- [ ] Has inputs/outputs section matching artifactAssignments from roster.json\\n- [ ] Has result codes matching roster.json\\n- [ ] Has status contract section\\n\\n### Content Quality\\n- [ ] Routing tables match routing.json entries exactly (no missing entries, no fabricated entries)\\n- [ ] Result codes match roster.json exactly\\n- [ ] Artifact assignments match roster.json exactly\\n- [ ] Domain invariants are relevant to this agent\'s role\\n- [ ] Instructions are specific enough to be actionable (not generic filler)\\n- [ ] Specialist agents have detailed work instructions (not just \\"do your job\\")\\n\\n### Anti-Patterns to Flag\\n- Generic/boilerplate content that doesn\'t reflect the specific agent\'s role\\n- Missing or incomplete routing tables for coordinators\\n- Fabricated routing entries not in routing.json\\n- Missing result codes\\n- Vague instructions (\\"ensure quality\\" without specifics)\\n- Coordinators doing substantive work instead of being pure routers\\n\\n## Output\\n\\nWrite your review findings to `.fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-prompt-reviewer/output.md` with:\\n1. Overall assessment (approved/rejected)\\n2. Per-agent issues (if any)\\n3. Summary statistics\\n\\nWrite your status to `.fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-prompt-reviewer/status.json`:\\n\\nIf ALL prompts pass:\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"agent\\": \\"fractal-factory-prompt-reviewer\\",\\n  \\"task_id\\": \\"pass4/prompt-review\\",\\n  \\"status\\": \\"completed\\",\\n  \\"result\\": \\"approved\\",\\n  \\"summary\\": \\"All 67 agent prompts pass review.\\",\\n  \\"artifacts\\": [\\"agents/fractal-factory-prompt-reviewer/status.json\\", \\"agents/fractal-factory-prompt-reviewer/output.md\\"],\\n  \\"next_hint\\": null,\\n  \\"iteration\\": 1\\n}\\n```\\n\\nIf ANY prompts fail:\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"agent\\": \\"fractal-factory-prompt-reviewer\\",\\n  \\"task_id\\": \\"pass4/prompt-review\\",\\n  \\"status\\": \\"completed\\",\\n  \\"result\\": \\"rejected\\",\\n  \\"summary\\": \\"N agents need revision: [list agent names]\\",\\n  \\"rejectedAgents\\": [\\"agent-name-1\\", \\"agent-name-2\\"],\\n  \\"artifacts\\": [\\"agents/fractal-factory-prompt-reviewer/status.json\\", \\"agents/fractal-factory-prompt-reviewer/output.md\\"],\\n  \\"next_hint\\": null,\\n  \\"iteration\\": 1\\n}\\n```\\n\\nBe thorough but fair. Minor formatting issues are not grounds for rejection. Focus on: missing routing entries, wrong result codes, missing artifact assignments, generic/empty content, purity violations."}',
