= {}\\nfor inv in invs:\\n    c = inv.get('classification', 'unknown')\\n    classifications[c] = classifications.get(c, 0) + 1\\nprint('=== INVARIANT CLASSIFICATIONS ===')\\nprint(json.dumps(classifications, indent=2))\\n\\n# Count invariants per subdomain\\nprint('\\\\n=== INVARIANTS PER SUBDOMAIN ===')\\nsd_inv_counts = {}\\nfor inv in invs:\\n    for sd in inv.get('affectedSubdomains', []):\\n        sd_inv_counts[sd] = sd_inv_counts.get(sd, 0) + 1\\nfor sd_id, cnt in sorted(sd_inv_counts.items()):\\n    print(f'  {sd_id}: {cnt} invariants')\\n\\n# Check exemplar patterns in more detail - pipeline-relevant ones\\nprint('\\\\n=== EXEMPLAR PATTERNS (pipeline-relevant) ===')\\nfor ep in dm.get('exemplarPatterns', []):\\n    if any(kw in ep['name'].lower() for kw in ['depth', 'coordinator', 'loop', 'convergence', 'pass', 'router', 'entry', 'dispatch']):\\n        print(f'\\\\n{ep[\\\\\\"name\\\\\\"]}:')\\n        print(f'  desc: {ep.get(\\\\\\"description\\\\\\",\\\\\\"\\\\\\")[:200]}')\\n        if 'applicability' in ep:\\n            print(f'  applicability: {ep[\\\\\\"applicability\\\\\\"][:200]}')\\n\\n# Existing assets detail\\nprint('\\\\n=== ALL EXISTING ASSETS ===')\\nfor a in dm.get('existingAssets', []):\\n    print(f'  [{a.get(\\\\\\"type\\\\\\")}] {a.get(\\\\\\"name\\\\\\")}: {a.get(\\\\\\"description\\\\\\",\\\\\\"\\\\\\")[:80]}')\\n\\" 2>&1\\n","description":"Deep-dive invariants and exemplars","initial_wait":15}}],"finish_reason":"stop"},{"role":"assistant","parts":[{"type":"reasoning","content":"Now I have a comprehensive understanding of the domain. Let me analyze the key characteristics:\\n\\n**Domain Characteristics Assessment:**\\n\\n1. **Discovery complexity**: HIGH - 14 subdomains, many with high complexity. They need different scanning approaches (creative vs. structural vs. cross-cutting).\\n\\n2. **Analysis depth**: HIGH - 81 invariants across 4 classifications (behavioral: 21, quality: 33, workflow: 13, structural: 14). SD-007 (chapter-drafting) has 47 invariants, SD-005 (plotting-and-outlining) has 41. These are complex behavioral/quality rules.\\n   \\n3. **Planning and execution complexity**: HIGH - The pipeline has strong sequential dependencies (worldbuilding before plotting, plotting before drafting) plus cross-cutting concerns that need weaving throughout. The work follows a writer→reviewer loop pattern adapted for creative work, with multiple such cycles needed. Verification requires checking 81 invariants through both checklists and oracle perspectives, making gap-hunting particularly valuable for creative domains.\\n\\n4. **Pipeline structure**: All 7 passes are justified given the scope. I'm running knowledge curation as a cold-start pre-pass, then discovery to scan subdomains and extract invariants, analysis for architecture and artifact design, planning for routing and test strategy, execution through the prompt-writing and review cycle, verification with dual validation, gap-hunting across coverage and infrastructure, and finally delivery.\\n\\nWait, I need to clarify what I'm actually designing here. The instructions ask for the pipeline for the produced agent system, but looking at the context and exemplar patterns, this is really about the factory pipeline that constructs the fantasy-writer system itself. The seven passes in context.json are the factory passes—discovery through delivery—that will build out the agent system, not the runtime pipeline the agent uses.\\n\\nNow I'm mapping out each factory pass with its purpose, coordinator, specialist agents, and parallelization potential. Discovery scans the domain and is already complete with four specialists. Analysis determines the architecture and artifact schemas with three independent analysis agents. I'm continuing through the remaining passes...\\n\\nPass 3 focuses on planning the agent roster and routing tables, which requires sequential work since routing depends on the roster decisions. Pass 4 handles writing all the prompts and infrastructure with a writer-reviewer loop that can retry up to ten times. Pass 5 validates everything against the invariants and architecture we've established.\\n\\nFor verification, I'm running two independent validators in parallel—one checking against a checklist and another providing an audit perspective. Pass 6 hunts for gaps across three independent dimensions: coverage, artifacts, and infrastructure`... 44774 more characters
