      'gen_ai.input.messages': `[{"role":"tool","parts":[{"type":"tool_call_response","id":"toolu_011BGUkNMWs7nksrj1kU6yBA","response":"Intent logged"}]},{"role":"tool","parts":[{"type":"tool_call_response","id":"toolu_01RsUdmVxd7wujg6HhZ5YmdQ","response":"agents\\narchitecture.json\\ncontext.json\\ndomain-brief.md\\ndomain-model.json\\ninvariants.md\\nknowledge-brief.json\\nmanifest.json\\nmeta\\nmeta-knowledge-reference.md\\nmeta-knowledge-templates.md\\nproduced-output\\nprogress.json\\nroster.json\\ntest-plan.json"}]},{"role":"tool","parts":[{"type":"tool_call_response","id":"toolu_01XrEbBpbBunHDrafrbLaRwN","response":"1. {\\n2.   \\"version\\": 1,\\n3.   \\"domain\\": {\\n4.     \\"name\\": \\"fantasy-writer\\",\\n5.     \\"description\\": \\"An autonomous multi-agent system that writes romantic fantasy fiction — from initial concept through worldbuilding, character development, plotting, prose style calibration, chapter drafting, adversarial phase gates, multi-pass revision, simulated multi-lens beta reading, and final polish. Designed for series production from day one: all artifacts are organized per-book with a shared series knowledge base enabling seamless sequel creation. Takes story ideas, reference fiction, and style samples as input. Produces complete, publication-quality romantic fantasy chapters with deeply subcategorized supporting artifacts (world bible split by geography/magic/politics/culture/history, per-character files, per-chapter outlines, per-lens beta feedback). Operates with a two-tier quality system: non-negotiable invariants that always apply, plus a craft toolbox of proven techniques selected per-story during concept/plotting and enforced by adversarial auditors.\\"\\n6.   },\\n7.   \\"target\\": {\\n8.     \\"outputDirectory\\": \\".fractal-factory/output/romantic-fantasy-writer\\",\\n9.     \\"namingPrefix\\": \\"romantic-fantasy-writer\\"\\n10.   },\\n11.   \\"inputs\\": {\\n12.     \\"domainBrief\\": \\".fractal-factory/domain-brief.md\\",\\n13.     \\"domainDocs\\": null,\\n14.     \\"exemplars\\": \\".fractals/fractal-factory/agents\\",\\n15.     \\"invariants\\": \\".fractal-factory/invariants.md\\",\\n16.     \\"constraints\\": null\\n17.   },\\n18.   \\"options\\": {\\n19.     \\"maxDepth\\": 3,\\n20.     \\"maxAgents\\": 80,\\n21.     \\"maxGapCycles\\": 10,\\n22.     \\"maxWriterReviewerRetries\\": 10,\\n23.     \\"pipelinePasses\\": [\\"discovery\\", \\"analysis\\", \\"planning\\", \\"execution\\", \\"verification\\", \\"gapHunting\\", \\"delivery\\"],\\n24.     \\"metaKnowledge\\": {\\n25.       \\"enabled\\": true,\\n26.       \\"domainSignalName\\": \\"craft\\"\\n27.     }\\n28.   }\\n29. }\\n30. "}]},{"role":"tool","parts":[{"type":"tool_call_response","id":"toolu_017fYUPCY2VJWvqAL89xsEQ2","response":"1. {\\n2.   \\"version\\": 1,\\n3.   \\"lastUpdated\\": \\"2026-03-16T00:25:00Z\\",\\n4.   \\"pipeline\\": {\\n5.     \\"passes\\": [\\n6.       {\\n7.         \\"pass\\": 0,\\n8.         \\"name\\": \\"knowledge-curation\\",\\n9.         \\"displayName\\": \\"Meta-Knowledge Curation\\",\\n10.         \\"purpose\\": \\"Curate accumulated meta-knowledge from prior factory runs into a task-relevant knowledge-brief.json. On cold start (first run), produce a minimal brief acknowledging no prior signals exist. On subsequent runs, distill craft-domain signals (prose patterns, worldbuilding consistency strategies, invariant enforcement lessons) into actionable guidance for downstream passes.\\",\\n11.         \\"entryCondition\\": \\"Always first — runs before any domain pass. Triggered unconditionally at pipeline start.\\",\\n12.         \\"exitCondition\\": \\"knowledge-brief.json written with coldStart flag set appropriately. Single-agent pass — no coordinator needed.\\",\\n13.         \\"coordinatorHint\\": null,\\n14.         \\"estimatedAgents\\": 1,\\n15.         \\"parallelizable\\": false,\\n16.         \\"notes\\": \\"Cold start for this run (first fantasy-writer session). Future runs will have craft-domain signals from the synthesis pass to curate. This pass is a no-op structurally but establishes the knowledge-brief.json contract for downstream consumers.\\"\\n17.       },\\n18.       {\\n19.         \\"pass\\": 1,\\n20.         \\"name\\": \\"discovery\\",\\n21.         \\"displayName\\": \\"Domain Discovery\\",\\n22.         \\"purpose\\": \\"Scan the fantasy-writer domain to build a comprehensive domain model: 14 subdomains (10 sequential creative phases + 4 cross-cutting concerns), behavioral/quality/workflow/structural invariants, reusable infrastructure assets, and exemplar hierarchy patterns. Produces the domain-model.json that all subsequent passes consume.\\",\\n23.         \\"entryCondition\\": \\"knowledge-brief.json exists (Pass 0 complete). No other preconditions.\\",\\n24.         \\"exitCondition\\": \\"All four discovery specialists (domain-scanner, invariant-extractor, asset-auditor, exemplar-analyzer) report status=completed. domain-model.json contains subdomains, invariants, existingAssets, and exemplarPatterns arrays. Discovery coordinator confirms completeness.\\",\\n25.         \\"coordinatorHint\\": \\"fractal-factory-discovery-coordinator\\",\\n26.         \\"estimatedAgents\\": 5,\\n27.         \\"parallelizable\\": true,\\n28.         \\"notes\\": \\"Four specialists scan independent aspects: (1) domain-scanner extracts 14 subdomains from domain-brief.md, (2) invariant-extractor classifies 81 invariants into behavioral/quality/workflow/structural, (3) asset-auditor catalogs 26 reusable assets (7 shared-includes, 11 skills, 3 agent-templates, 4 tools, 1 MCP server), (4) exemplar-analyzer extracts 20 patterns from the fractal-factory exemplar family. All run in parallel under the coordinator. ALREADY COMPLETED in this run.\\"\\n29.       },\\n30.       {\\n31.         \\"pass\\": 2,\\n32.         \\"name\\": \\"analysis\\",\\n33.         \\"displayName\\": \\"Architecture Analysis\\",\\n34.         \\"purpose\\": \\"Analyze the discovered domain model to determine three architectural decisions: (1) pipeline pass structure and re-entry rules for the produced fantasy-writer system, (2) shared artifact schemas and data flow contracts between agents, (3) hierarchy depth (depth-2 vs depth-3) per coordinator based on subdomain complexity. These three analyses are independent and inform the planning pass.\\",\\n35.         \\"entryCondition\\": \\"Pass 1 complete — domain-model.json exists with all four sections populated. Discovery coordinator status=completed.\\",\\n36.         \\"exitCondition\\": \\"All three analysis specialists (pipeline-architect, artifact-designer, depth-analyzer) report status=completed. architecture.json contains populated pipeline, artifacts, and depth sections.\\",\\n37.         \\"coordinatorHint\\": \\"fractal-factory-analysis-coordinator\\",\\n38.         \\"estimatedAgents\\": 4,\\n39.         \\"parallelizable\\": true,\\n40.         \\"notes\\": \\"Three independent analyses run in parallel: pipeline-architect designs the produced system's pass structure (this agent — designing the factory pipeline); artifact-designer maps the 30+ artifact types across 14 subdomains into schemas with read-modify-write contracts; depth-analyzer evaluates each subdomain's complexity against the maxDepth=3 budget and maxAgents=80 ceiling. The high complexity of 7 subdomains (worldbuilding, character-development, plotting, chapter-drafting, revision, beta-reading, adversarial-consistency) plus 81 invariants strongly suggests depth-3 is needed for creative phases. CURRENTLY IN PROGRESS.\\"\\n41.       },\\n42.       {\\n43.         \\"pass\\": 3,\\n44.         \\"name\\": \\"planning\\",\\n45.         \\"displayName\\": \\"Roster & Routing Planning\\",\\n46.         \\"purpose\\": \\"Plan the complete agent roster (up to 80 agents), routing tables for every coordinator and the orchestrator, and golden test scenarios. Roster planning assigns agents to the 14 subdomains respecting hierarchy depth decisions. Routing planning defines the markdown routing tables with read/condition/action columns. Test planning creates scenarios covering the creative pipeline end-to-end, series production, adversarial gate failures, and craft-tool enforcement.\\",\\n47.         \\"entryCondition\\": \\"Pass 2 complete — architecture.json fully populated with pipeline, artifacts, and depth sections. All three analysis agents report status=completed.\\",\\n48.         \\"exitCondition\\": \\"roster.json contains all agents with assigned levels, parents, children, result codes, and artifact assignments. routing-tables.json or equivalent contains routing tables for every coordinator. test-scenarios.json contains golden test cases. Planning coordinator confirms completeness.\\",\\n49.         \\"coordinatorHint\\": \\"fractal-factory-planning-coordinator\\",\\n50.         \\"estimatedAgents\\": 4,\\n51.         \\"parallelizable\\": false,\\n52.         \\"notes\\": \\"Sequential dispatch required: roster-planner runs first (routing and tests depend on knowing agent names and hierarchy). Then routing-planner builds tables using the roster. Finally test-planner creates scenarios referencing both roster and routes. The 14-subdomain, 80-agent budget with depth-3 hierarchy makes this the most complex planning pass. Key decisions: how to allocate the agent budget across 10 sequential phases + 4 cross-cutting concerns, how many specialist writers vs. reviewers per creative phase, and how adversarial auditors integrate as sub-phase gates.\\"\\n53.       },\\n54.       {\\n55.         \\"pass\\": 4,\\n56.         \\"name\\": \\"execution\\",\\n57.         \\"displayName\\": \\"Prompt Writing & Infrastructure\\",\\n58.         \\"purpose\\": \\"Write all agent prompt files (.agent.md) following the universal prompt template, and produce infrastructure files (bootstrap script, artifact schemas, skill stubs, golden test files). Uses a bounded writer→reviewer loop: promp