30+ artifact schemas with detailed field specifications, and depth decisions for each coordinator)\n\n3. Status at end of reading phase\n   - All three critical reference files fully loaded into context\n   - No reviewer feedback document read yet (from prompt-reviewer/output.md)\n   - No prompts rewritten; work hasn't begun yet\n</history>\n\n<work_done>\nNo files created or modified yet. This conversation is at the research/preparation phase.\n\nFiles read (not modified):\n- `.fractal-factory/domain-model.json` — Contains 81 domain invariants with full text, affecting subdomains, verification strategies, and classification\n- `.fractal-factory/roster.json` — Contains all 67 agents with specifications: level, parent/children hierarchy, pass assignments, result codes, artifact reads/writes, antiLaziness flags, status (designed/written/reviewed/verified/blocked)\n- `.fractal-factory/architecture.json` — Contains complete pipeline (7 passes + knowledge curation pass 0), artifact schemas (30+ types), re-entry rules, convergence logic, and depth decisions\n\nWork completed:\n- [x] Read domain-model.json to understand 81 invariants and their subdomain mappings\n- [x] Read roster.json to understand agent hierarchy and artifact contracts\n- [x] Read architecture.json to understand pipeline structure and artifact schemas\n- [ ] Read prompt-reviewer/output.md for specific rejection feedback (NOT YET DONE)\n- [ ] Begin rewriting 47 agent prompts (NOT STARTED)\n- [ ] Create/update status.json (NOT DONE)\n- [ ] Create/update output.md with summary of changes (NOT DONE)\n</work_done>\n\n<technical_details>\n**Architectural Patterns (from architecture.json review):**\n- The fantasy-writer system uses a depth-2 and depth-3 hierarchy pattern (exemplar from fractal-factory)\n- Depth-2 coordinators: concept, style, revision, polish (simple structures, 2-4 specialists each)\n- Depth-3 coordinators: worldbuilding, character, plotting, drafting, beta-reading (complex structures with sub