ions, climate zones, landmarks, travel methods/distances, how settings enable or constrain the romantic relationship.',\\n        'process_steps': [\\n            '1. Read story-concept.json — extract genre, tone, scale (intimate vs epic)',\\n            '2. Design the world\\\\'s geography: continents, countries, major regions',\\n            '3. For each significant location in the story, document: name, type (capital, village, dungeon), climate, significance to plot, and why romance happens there',\\n            '4. Map connections between locations: how do characters travel? What are travel times/dangers?',\\n            '5. Identify 3-5 key symbolic locations (meeting places for romantic moments, battlegrounds, refuges)',\\n            '6. Document physical constraints: mountains, oceans, deserts that divide or connect factions/characters',\\n            '7. Cross-reference world-bible/culture.json and world-bible/magic-system.json once available — geography must align with culture and magic',\\n            '8. Write world-bible/geography.json with locations (ID: LOC-NNN), travel rules, symbolic significance',\\n            '9. Include downstream reference: relative path to story-concept.json (per INV-029)',\\n            '10. Mark as internally consistent per INV-002 — all locations described consistently'\\n        ],\\n        'invariants': ['INV-002', 'INV-029'],\\n        'artifact_reads': ['story-concept.json'],\\n        'artifact_writes': ['world-bible/geography.json'],\\n        'result_codes': ['completed', 'blocked'],\\n    },\\n\\n    'romantic-fantasy-writer-culture-builder': {\\n        'role': 'Design cultural norms, customs, social hierarchies, naming conventions, religions, taboos. Prevents anachronisms per INV-018 and constrains character behavior.',\\n        'process_steps': [\\n            '1. Read story-concept.json for tone and setting type',\\n            '2. Read world-bible/geography.json to understand regional divisions',\\n          