ctures)',\\n            '3. Read romance-arc-design.json to understand romance pacing needs',\\n            '4. Review available structural frameworks: three-act, Save the Cat (12-beat), Hero\\\\'s Journey (12-stage), custom variants',\\n            '5. Assess which framework best fits this story: three-act is traditional, Save the Cat emphasizes emotional beats, Hero\\\\'s Journey emphasizes transformation',\\n            '6. For chosen framework: define act boundaries and key turning point chapters',\\n            '7. Map story beats to chapters based on estimated chapter count',\\n            '8. Ensure stakes escalate through acts per INV-044/T6',\\n            '9. Write plot-structure.json with framework, acts, key beats (ID: BEAT-NNN), subplots (ID: SUB-NNN)',\\n            '10. Include upstream references to story-concept.json, craft-profile.json, romance-arc-design.json (per INV-029)'\\n        ],\\n        'invariants': ['INV-044'],\\n        'artifact_reads': ['story-concept.json', 'craft-profile.json', 'romance-arc-design.json'],\\n        'artifact_writes': ['plot-structure.json'],\\n        'result_codes': ['completed', 'blocked'],\\n    },\\n\\n    'romantic-fantasy-writer-dual-arc-builder': {\\n        'role': 'Interleave fantasy plot and romance arc per chapter, mapping key beats from each to show where they reinforce or counterpoint each other (INV-050/T12).',\\n        'process_steps': [\\n            '1. Read plot-structure.json and extract all fantasy plot beats (ID: BEAT-NNN)',\\n            '2. Read romance-arc-design.json and map romance stages to chapters',\\n            '3. For each chapter from 1 to estimated total: assign which fantasy beat(s) occur and which romance stage(s) are active',\\n            '4. Identify interleave patterns: some chapters are fantasy-dominant, some romance-dominant, some balanced',\\n            '5. For each chapter, document the relationship between arcs: do they reinforce (e.g., both hit climax together)? Do they counterpoint (high romance while fantasy stalls)?',\\n            '6. Ensure romance doesn\\\\'t disappear in pure action chapters — at least a beat or complication per chapter (INV-001)',\\n            '7. Ensure fantasy stakes never disappear in romance-heavy chapters',\\n            '8. Write dual-arc-timeline.json with per-chapter beat assignments and interleave ratios',\\n            '9. Include upstream references to plot-structure.json and romance-arc-design.json (per INV-029)',\\n            '10. Verify chapter count matches story-concept.json estimate'\\n        ],\\n        'invariants': ['INV-001', 'INV-050'],\\n        'artifact_reads': ['plot-structure.json', 'romance-arc-design.json', 'story-concept.json'],\\n        'artifact_writes': ['dual-arc-timeline.json'],\\n        'result_codes': ['completed', 'blocked'],\\n    },\\n\\n    'romantic-fantasy-writer-tension-mapper': {\\n        'role': 'Create pacing chart showing tension rise-and-fall across all chapters to avoid flat stretches per INV-020.',\\n        'process_steps': [\\n            '1. Read plot-structure.json, dual-arc-timeline.json, and romance-arc-design.json',\\n            '2. For each chapter: assign tension level (1-10 scale) based on plot beats, romance escalation, and pacing needs',\\n            '3. Consider four tension types: action/plot tension, emotional tension, romantic tension, mystery/anticipation',\\n            '4. Verify no 3+ consecutive chapters have the same tension level (INV-020) — tension must vary',\\n            '5. Identify peaks (climactic chapters) and valleys (recovery/introspection chapters)',\\n            '6. Ensure pattern feels natural: peaks build through increasing tension, valleys provide breathing room',\\n            '7. Check blackmoment chapter for lowest emotional tension (allows darkest moment)',\\n            '8. Verify final chapters build to crescendo for ending',\\n            '9. Write tension-map.json with per-chapter tension levels, types, peaks/valleys, and pacing notes',\\n            '10. Include upstream references to plot-structure.json and dual-arc-timeline.json (per INV-029)'\\n        ],\\n        'invariants': ['INV-020', 'INV-051'],\\n        'artifact_reads': ['plot-structure.json', 'dual-arc-timeline.json', 'romance-arc-design.json'],\\n        'artifact_writes': ['tension-map.json'],\\n        'result_codes': ['completed', 'blocked'],\\n    },\\n\\n    'romantic-fantasy-writer-chapter-outliner': {\\n        'role': 'Produce per-chapter outlines with POV character, scene goals, conflict, emotional arc, and beat assignments. Required before drafting per INV-010.',\\n        'process_steps': [\\n            '1. Read plot-structure.json, dual-arc-timeline.json, tension-map.json for macro structure',\\n            '2. Read romance-arc-design.json for romance stage per chapter',\\n            '3. For each chapter N in sequence:',\\n            '   a. Assign POV character from characters/index.json',\\n            '   b. Document POV transition motivation if switching POV (INV-072)',\\n            '   c. Extract scene goals from plot outline and assign to scenes',\\n            '   d. Define the chapter\\\\'s central conflict (fantasy and/or romantic)',\\n            '   e. Map emotional arc for the POV character (starting emotion → ending emotion)',\\n            '   f. Assign fantasy plot beats and romance stage beats for this chapter',\\n            '   g. Define chapter hook type and close type per INV-060/T22 (vary hook types across chapters)',\\n            '   h. Estimate target word count',\\n            '4. Write chapter-outlines/{N}.json for each chapter with scenes (ID: SCN-NNN), emotional arc, beat assignments',\\n            '5. Ensure outlines explicitly contain required fields per INV-010: POV, goal, conflict, emotional arc, beats',\\n            '6. Include upstream references (per INV-029)',\\n            '7. Complete all outlines BEFORE any drafting begins (INV-010)'\\n  