'   - Scene structure per selected tools (T1/T2/T3/T4 if selected)',\\n            '   - Show don\\\\'t tell for emotions (INV-005)',\\n            '   - No info-dumping (INV-007)',\\n            '   - Dialogue naturalism (INV-019)',\\n            '   - Tension throughout (INV-035)',\\n            '10. After drafting, update:',\\n            '    - chapters/{N}/draft.md with prose',\\n            '    - chapters/{N}/metadata.json with structured metadata (scene breakdown, craft tool compliance, word count)',\\n            '    - continuity-tracker.json with new character positions, timeline events, knowledge gains',\\n            '    - foreshadowing-ledger.json with new plants and payoffs identified',\\n            '11. Write status.json with result=completed or blocked'\\n        ],\\n        'invariants': ['INV-002', 'INV-003', 'INV-005', 'INV-007', 'INV-010', 'INV-011', 'INV-019', 'INV-020', 'INV-021', 'INV-035', 'INV-039', 'INV-040', 'INV-041', 'INV-042'],\\n        'artifact_reads': ['chapter-outlines/{N}.json', 'characters/{CHAR-NNN}.json', 'style-guide.json', 'world-bible/*', 'continuity-tracker.json', 'foreshadowing-ledger.json', 'dual-arc-timeline.json', 'craft-profile.json'],\\n        'artifact_writes': ['chapters/{N}/draft.md', 'chapters/{N}/metadata.json', 'continuity-tracker.json', 'foreshadowing-ledger.json'],\\n        'result_codes': ['completed', 'blocked'],\\n    },\\n\\n    'romantic-fantasy-writer-pov-voice-maintainer': {\\n        'role': 'Review drafted chapter for POV voice consistency and distinctiveness, ensuring the voice fingerprint is maintained throughout (INV-003, INV-034, INV-015).',\\n        'process_steps': [\\n            '1. Read chapters/{N}/draft.md and the POV character profile from characters/{CHAR-NNN}.json',\\n            '2. Perform the 3-4 sentence test per INV-034: strip character names from 3-4 sentence blocks — is the POV identifiable?',\\n            '3. Compare voice fingerprint against actual prose:',\\n            '   - Sentence length: measure average length, range, rhythm',\\n            '   - Vocabulary register: count elevated vs simple word choices — does it match fingerprint?',\\n            '   - Metaphor use: count metaphors, assess type — does density match fingerprint?',\\n            '   - Emotional expression style: how are emotions shown? Direct declaration, physical sensation, action, internal reaction? Match fingerprint?',\\n            '   - Thought patterns: are thoughts analytical, intuitive, or emotional? Match fingerprint?',\\n            '4. Flag any passages that sound like a different character',\\n            '5. Flag any narrative voice bleeding in that breaks POV distinctiveness',\\n            '6. For dialogue: check that this character\\\\'s speech patterns (word choice, contractions, length, topics) are consistent with their established voice',\\n            '7. Compare against other POV characters already drafted — verify distinctiveness per INV-034',\\n            '8. Make micro-edits to maintain voice without changing plot/meaning',\\n            '9. Update chapters/{N}/draft.md with voice corrections',\\n            '10. Write output notes documenting voice checks performed and any adjustments made'\\n        ],\\n        'invariants': ['INV-003', 'INV-015', 'INV-034', 'INV-055'],\\n        'artifact_reads': ['chapters/{N}/draft.md', 'characters/{CHAR-NNN}.json', 'style-guide.json'],\\n        'artifact_writes': ['chapters/{N}/draft.md'],\\n        'result_codes': ['completed', 'blocked'],\\n    },\\n\\n    'romantic-fantasy-writer-continuity-integrator': {\\n        'role': 'Verify chapter draft against continuity tracker for character positions, timeline progression, naming consistency, and knowledge state per INV-011, INV-016, INV-018, INV-056/T18.',\\n        'process_steps': [\\n            '1. Read chapters/{N}/draft.md to extract all factual claims',\\n            '2. Read continuity-tracker.json to verify:',\\n            '   a. Character locations: are all character positions consistent with previous state?',\\n            '   b. Timeline: are in-world time progressions consistent? No characters in two places at once?',\\n            '   c. Naming: are all character/place/term names spelled consistently?',\\n            '   d. World rules: do descriptions match world-bible/* definitions?',\\n            '3. Read information-asymmetry-map.json to verify per INV-056/T18:',\\n            '   - Does this chapter reveal information only to POV character, not to reader? (check for accidental info leaks)',\\n            '   - Does chapter respect character knowledge state? (no character using information they don\\\\'t know)',\\n            '4. Read world-bible/* files:',\\n            '   - geography: are locations described consistently?',\\n            '   - magic: are magic rules honored? No violations of hard magic rules?',\\n            '   - culture: are cultural norms honored? No anachronisms per INV-018?',\\n            '   - politics: are faction relationships and power dynamics consistent?',\\n            '5. Cross-check chapter metadata (chapters/{N}/metadata.json) against continuity tracker',\\n            '6. Flag any discrepancies as \\\"continuity violation\\\" with specific location and reference',\\n            '7. Suggest corrections for continuity violations',\\n            '8. Update chapters/{N}/draft.md with corrections if minor',\\n            '9. Return chapters/{N}/draft.md and update status.json',\\n            '10. Note: major contradictions may warrant drafting revisions — flag clearly'\\n        ],\\n        'invariants': ['INV-002', 'INV-011', 'INV-016', 'INV-018', 'INV-056'],\\n        'artifact_reads': ['chapters/{N}/draft.md', 'continuity-tracker.json', 'information-asymmetry-map.json', 'world-bible/*'],\\n        'artifact_writes': ['chapters/{N}/draft.md'],\\n        'result_codes': ['completed', 'blocked'],\\n    },\\n\\n    'romantic-fantasy-writer-craft-enforcer': {\\n        'role': 'Verify chapter draft adheres to all selected craft tools from craft-profile.json. Adversarial auditor role — anti-laziness enforcement required.',\\n        'process_steps': [\\n            '1. Read craft-profile.json and load selected tools with their enforcement phases',\\n            '2. For this chapter, identify which selected tools require enforcement',\\n            '3. Read chapters/{N}/draft.md and chapters/{N}/metadata.json',\\n            '4. For each selected tool active in this phase:',\\n            '   - T1 (Scene-Sequel): verify Goal→Conflict→Disaster and Reaction→Dilemma→Decision structures per outline',\\n            '   - T2 (Value Shifts): verify each scene shifts at least one value (emotional/relational/informational/situational)',\\n            '   - T3 (Five Commandments): verify each scene contains required commandments where applicable',\\n            '   - T4 (Try-Fail): verify major challenges show at least 2 failed approaches before success',\\n            '   - T5 (Tone Contract): verify tonal consistency with opening chapters\\\\' promise',\\n            '   - T6 (Stakes Escalation): verify this chapter\\\\'s stakes are appropriate to its act',\\n            '   - T7 (Black Moment): if this is the black moment chapter, verify it feels genuinely threatening',\\n            '   - T8 (Internal Resistance): verify romantic obstacles include internal/psychological elements',\\n            '   - T9 (Subtext): verify charged dialogue has subtext; characters don\\\\'t say exactly what they mean',\\n            '   - T10 (Sanderson\\\\'s Law): verify hard magic rules honored; soft magic doesn\\\\'t solve conflicts',\\n            '   - T13 (Tension Mapping): verify tension level matches tension-map.json for this chapter',\\n            '   - T14 (MRU): verify action sequences follow Motivation→Reaction (feeling→reflex→rational)',\\n            '   - T15 (Foreshadowing): verify foreshadowing ledger accurately tracks plants/payoffs',\\n            '   - T17 (Voice Fingerprint): verify POV voice matches fingerprint',\\n            '   - T18 (Info Asymmetry): verify information is revealed appropriately per character knowledge',\\n            '   - T20 (Emotional Throughline): verify POV emotional state shows variety and escalation',\\n            '   - T22 (Hook/Close): verify hook and close types are distinct from adjacent chapters',\\n            '   - T23 (Mystery Box): verify active unresolved questions maintained per inventory',\\n            '5. Document violations with specific chapter line references',\\n            '6. Flag critical violations (tool not applied at all) vs major (partially applied)',\\n            '7. Write output documenting all tool compliance findings',\\n            '8. Do NOT pass without checking every selected tool per anti-laziness mandate'\\n        ],\\n        'invariants': ['INV-039', 'INV-040', 'INV-041', 'INV-042', 'INV-043', 'INV-044', 'INV-045', 'INV-046', 'INV-047', 'INV-048', 'INV-050', 'INV-051', 'INV-052', 'INV-053', 'INV-054', 'INV-055', 'INV-056', 'INV-057', 'INV-058', 'INV-060', 'INV-061', 'INV-062'],\\n        'artifact_reads': ['chapters/{N}/draft.md', 'chapters/{N}/metadata.json', 'craft-profile.json', 'chapter-outlines/{N}.json'],\\n        'artifact_writes': ['chapters/{N}/draft.md', 'agents/craft-enforcer/output.md'],\\n        'result_codes': ['completed', 'blocked'],\\n    },\\n\\n    'romantic-fantasy-writer-developmental-editor': {\\n        'role': 'Perform developmental edit on chapter: plot holes, pacing issues, motivation clarity, arc satisfaction, thematic coherence. First of three mandatory review passes per INV-013.',\\n        'process_steps': [\\n            '1. Read chapters/{N}/draft.md and extract plot events and character motivations',\\n            '2. Read chapter-outlines/{N}.json and plot-structure.json to verify outline adherence',\\n            '3. Read dual-arc-timeline.json to confirm fantasy and romance beats are present',\\n            '4. Read romance-arc-design.json to verify emotional beats match arc stage',\\n            '5. Check for plot holes:',\\n            '   - Are character motivations clear? Why do characters make the choices they make?',\\n            '   - Are cause-and-effect chains clear? Does A lead to B lead to C?',\\n            '   - Are coincidences explained or lampshaded, not convenient?',\\n            '   - Is no deus ex machina per INV-009?',\\n            '6. Check pacing:',\\n            '   - Does chapter match tension-map.json tension level?',\\n            '   - Are slow/fast passages balanced?',\\n            '   - Is exposition woven in or info-dumped (INV-007)?',\\n            '7. Check emotional beats:',\\n            '   - Are beats earned per INV-004 (buildup before emotional payoff)?',\\n            '   - Do emotions escalate toward chapter goal?',\\n            '   - Is emotional arc realized in prose?',\\n            '8. Check arc satisfaction:',\\n            '   - Does the chapter advance character and relationship arcs per romance-arc-design.json?',\\n            '   - Are stakes appropriate to this chapter\\\\'s place in story?',\\n            '9. Identify kill-your-darlings per INV-049/T11/INV-081: beautiful passages that don\\\\'t serve story',\\n            '10. Document findings in revision-reports/{N}/developmental.json with severity levels (critical/major/minor) and specific line references'\\n        ],\\n        'invariants': ['INV-004', 'INV-006', 'INV-009', 'INV-007', 'INV-020', 'INV-037', 'INV-049'],\\n        'artifact_reads': ['chapters/{N}/draft.md', 'chapter-outlines/{N}.json', 'plot-structure.json', 'dual-arc-timeline.json', 'romance-arc-design.json', 'tension-map.json'],\\n        'artifact_writes': ['revision-reports/{N}/developmental.json'],\\n        'result_codes': ['completed', 'blocked'],\\n    },\\n\\n    'romantic-fantasy-writer-line-editor': {\\n        'role': 'Perform line edit on chapter: prose quality, voice distinctness, cliché detection, show-vs-tell, repetition, dialogue naturalism. Second mandatory review pass.',\\n        'process_steps': [\\n            '1. Read chapters/{N}/draft.md sentence-by-sentence',\\n            '2. Read style-guide.json and characters/{CHAR-NNN}.json for voice fingerprints',\\n            '3. Check prose quality per INV-017 (prose quality floor):',\\n            '   - Count clichés (maintain list of common fantasy clichés) — max 2 per chapter',\\n            '   - Count adverbs — reasonable density, not excessive',\\n            '   - Count passive voice — should be <15% typically',\\n            '   - Assess sentence variety: mix of short/long, simple/complex',\\n            '4. Check voice consistency per INV-015:',\\n            '   - Does voice match POV character fingerprint throughout?',\\n            '   - Flag passages that sound like different character or narrative voice bleeding in',\\n            '5. Check show-vs-tell per INV-005:',\\n            '   - Key emotional moments should be shown through action/sensation/reaction, not told (\\\"she felt angry\\\" → show the anger)',\\n            '   - Background/summary can be told; key scenes should be shown',\\n            '6. Check dialogue naturalism per INV-019:',\\n            '   - Do characters interrupt, trail off, use contractions?',\\n            '   - Is dialogue realistic (people talk past each other, hesitate, etc.)?',\\n            '   - Flag overly philosophical monologues or exposition disguised as dialogue',\\n            '7. Check repetition:',\\n            '   - Repeated words/phrases within paragraphs (unintentional)',\\n            '   - Repeated sentence structures too close together',\\n            '   - Over-used descriptors or metaphors',\\n            '8. Check for micro-tension per INV-035: every half-page has at least one tension source?',\\n            '9. Suggest line-specific improvements without changing plot',\\n            '10. Document findings in revision-reports/{N}/line-edit.json with severity, line references, and suggested improvements'\\n        ],\\n        'invariants': ['INV-005', 'INV-015', 'INV-017', 'INV-019', 'INV-035'],\\n        'artifact_reads': ['chapters/{N}/draft.md', 'style-guide.json', 'characters/{CHAR-NNN}.json'],\\n        'artifact_writes': ['revision-reports/{N}/line-edit.json'],\\n        'result_codes': ['completed', 'blocked'],\\n    },\\n\\n    'romantic-fantasy-writer-copy-editor': {\\n        'role': 'Perform copy edit on chapter: grammar, naming consistency, timeline accuracy, factual accuracy within world rules, formatting. Third mandatory review pass.',\\n        'process_steps': [\\n            '1. Read chapters/{N}/draft.md for grammar and mechanics:',\\n            '   - Spelling, punctuation, capitalization',\\n            '   - Dialogue punctuation per style guide',\\n            '   - Consistent formatting (italics for thoughts/spells/etc)',\\n            '2. Check naming consistency per INV-018:',\\n            '   - All character/place/term names match continuity-tracker.json canonical spellings',\\n            '   - No accidental misspellings or alternate spellings',\\n            '3. Check timeline accuracy:',\\n            '   - Chapter timeline matches continuity-tracker.json?',\\n            '   - In-world dates/time progressions consistent?',\\n            '   - No time skips without explanation?',\\n            '4. Check factual accuracy within world rules per INV-018:',\\n            '   - Geography descriptions match world-bible/geography.json?',\\n            '   - Magic descriptions match world-bible/magic-system.json (hard magic rules especially)?',\\n            '   - Cultural details match world-bible/culture.json?',\\n            '   - Political references match world-bible/politics.json?',\\n            '   - Historical references match world-bible/history.json?',\\n            '5. Check character consistency:',\\n            '   - Physical descriptions match character profiles',\\n            '   - Character positions match continuity tracker',\\n            '   - No contradictions with previously established facts',\\n            '6. Flag anachronisms per INV-018: modern concepts/slang that don\\\\'t exist in this world',\\n            '7. Format check: scene breaks, chapter heading, consistent spacing',\\n            '8. Document findings in revision-reports/{N}/copy-edit.json with severity, line references, and corrections'\\n        ],\\n        'invariants': ['INV-002', 'INV-011', 'INV-018'],\\n        'artifact_reads': ['chapters/{N}/draft.md', 'continuity-tracker.json', 'world-bible/*'],\\n        'artifact_writes': ['revision-reports/{N}/copy-edit.json'],\\n        'result_codes': ['completed', 'blocked'],\\n    },\\n\\n    'romantic-fantasy-writer-chapter-reviser': {\\n        'role': 'Apply all revision reports to chapter draft, creating revised version. Every change must cite which finding prompted it per INV-014. Traceability is required.',\\n        'process_steps': [\\n            '1. Read chapters/{N}/draft.md',\\n            '2. Read revision-reports/{N}/developmental.json and extract findings',\\n            '3. Read revision-reports/{N}/line-edit.json and extract findings',\\n            '4. Read revision-reports/{N}/copy-edit.json and extract findings',\\n            '5. Prioritize findings: critical first, major second, minor third',\\n            '6. Apply critical fixes (plot holes, consistency violations, missing elements)',\\n            '7. Apply major fixes (pacing issues, voice drift, show-vs-tell problems)',\\n            '8. Apply minor fixes (typos, dialogue tags, small rewordings)',\\n            '9. For each change made, note the revision in the frontmatter: revisionVersion increments, findingsAddressed array lists finding IDs',\\n            '10. Write revised prose to chapters/{N}/revised.md with revision history in frontmatter',\\n            '11. Per INV-014 \\\"Revision Traceability\\\": every change must cite the finding that prompted it — include in frontmatter or inline comments',\\n            '12. Beta synthesis findings (if they triggered revision cycle) should also be cited',\\n            '13. Write status.json with result=completed or blocked'\\n        ],\\n        'invariants': ['INV-013', 'INV-014'],\\n        'artifact_reads': ['chapters/{N}/draft.md', 'revision-reports/{N}/*', 'beta-synthesis/{N}.json'],\\n        'artifact_writes': ['chapters/{N}/revised.md'],\\n        'result_codes': ['completed', 'blocked'],\\n    },\\n\\n    'romantic-fantasy-writer-romance-beta-reader': {\\n        'role': 'Evaluate chapter from romance reader perspective: emotional satisfaction, chemistry, pacing of romantic beats, HFN/HEA trajectory, heat level consistency, relationship believability.',\\n        'process_steps': [\\n            '1. Read chapters/{N}/revised.md as a romance reader — what\\\\'s the emotional experience?',\\n            '2. Read romance-arc-design.json to understand expected romance stage and beats for this chapter',\\n            '3. Assess emotional satisfaction:',\\n            '   - Do romantic moments feel earned (buildup per INV-004)?',\\n            '   - Is chemistry between leads present and growing?',\\n            '   - Are emotional escalations believable?',\\n            '4. Check heat level consistency: does intimacy level match story-config.json constraints?',\\n            '5. Check relationship trajectory:',\\n            '   - Is this chapter\\\\'s romance beat appropriate to arc stage?',\\n            '   - Does relationship progress plausibly or stall without reason?',\\n            '6. Check for earned vulnerability per INV-059/T21: if vulnerability moment, does it surprise and deepen bond?',\\n            '7. Assess black moment (if applicable): does the romantic break feel devastating enough?',\\n            '8. Check for deus ex machina in romance resolution (INV-009): is reconciliation earned or convenient?',\\n            '9. Document findings in beta-feedback/{N}/romance-lens.json with severity levels, arc progress assessment',\\n            '10. Include arcProgressCheck: is romance on track for HEA/HFN per outline?'\\n        ],\\n        'invariants': ['INV-001', 'INV-004', 'INV-008', 'INV-021', 'INV-045', 'INV-059'],\\n        'artifact_reads': ['chapters/{N}/revised.md', 'romance-arc-design.json', 'characters/{CHAR-NNN}.json'],\\n        'artifact_writes': ['beta-feedback/{N}/romance-lens.json'],\\n        'result_codes': ['completed', 'blocked'],\\n    },\\n\\n    'romantic-fantasy-writer-fantasy-beta-reader': {\\n        'role': 'Evaluate chapter from fantasy reader perspective: worldbuilding immersion, magic system consistency, plot logic, action sequences, world rules adherence.',\\n        'process_steps': [\\n            '1. Read chapters/{N}/revised.md as a fantasy reader — is the world immersive? Do magic and world feel consistent?',\\n            '2. Read world-bible/* files to verify details match',\\n            '3. Check worldbuilding immersion:',\\n            '   - Are descriptive details evocative without info-dumping (INV-007)?',\\n            '   - Does geography feel real and consistent with earlier chapters?',\\n            '   - Are cultural details woven in naturally?',\\n            '4. Check magic consistency:',\\n            '   - Are magic rules honored per world-bible/magic-system.json?',\\n            '   - Hard magic: are costs/limitations respected?',\\n            '   - Is magic used per Sanderson\\\\'s Law (INV-048/T10): hard magic with clear rules, soft magic not solving conflicts?',\\n            '   - No deus ex machina per INV-009?',\\n            '5. Check plot logic:',\\n            '   - Do character decisions make sense in world context?',\\n            '   - Are political/cultural consequences considered?',\\n            '   - Is cause-and-effect clear?',\\n            '6. Check world rules consistency per INV-002:',\\n            '   - Geography matches continuity tracker and maps',\\n            '   - Magic mechanics consistent with established rules',\\n            '   - Political alliances and power dynamics consistent',\\n            '   - Cultural norms honored (no anachronisms per INV-018)',\\n            '7. Check action sequences (if present):',\\n            '   - Is motion clear and followable?',\\n            '   - Are magic powers used consistently with system?',\\n            '   - Do consequences of action feel real?',\\n            '8. Document findings in beta-feedback/{N}/fantasy-lens.json with immersion score, magic consistency assessment'\\n        ],\\n        'invariants': ['INV-002', 'INV-007', 'INV-009', 'INV-018', 'INV-048'],\\n        'artifact_reads': ['chapters/{N}/revised.md', 'world-bible/*', 'continuity-tracker.json'],\\n        'artifact_writes': ['beta-feedback/{N}/fantasy-lens.json'],\\n        'result_codes': ['completed', 'blocked'],\\n    },\\n\\n    'romantic-fantasy-writer-craft-beta-reader': {\\n        'role': 'Evaluate chapter from craft reader perspective: adherence to selected craft tools, scene structure, pacing, foreshadowing, technique execution.',\\n        'process_steps': [\\n            '1. Read chapters/{N}/revised.md and chapters/{N}/metadata.json',\\n            '2. Read craft-profile.json to understand selected tools',\\n            '3. For each selected craft tool, verify application in this chapter:',\\n            '   - Scene structure tools (T1/T2/T3) applied correctly',\\n            '   - Try-fail cycles evident if applicable (T4)',\\n            '   - Tone contract maintained (T5)',\\n            '   - Stakes escalation appropriate to chapter position (T6)',\\n            '   - Scene values shifting (T2)',\\n            '   - Subtext in charged dialogue (T9)',\\n            '   - Voice fingerprint maintained (T17)',\\n            '   - Foreshadowing plants traceable (T15)',\\n            '   - Emotional throughline showed (T20)',\\n            '   - Hook and close types varied (T22)',\\n            '4. Check scene pacing:',\\n            '   - Does chapter match tension-map.json tension level?',\\n            '   - Are scenes properly paced (not rushing important moments, not dwelling on exposition)?',\\n            '5. Check foreshadowing:',\\n            '   - Are new plants placed appropriately and subtly?',\\n            '   - Are promised payoffs being delivered (foreshadowing-ledger.json)?',\\n            '   - Are callbacks to earlier foreshadowing present?',\\n            '6. Assess craft technique execution:',\\n            '   - Dialogue function tagged correctly (each exchange 3+ lines has narrative purpose)?',\\n            '   - MRU ordering in action sequences (feeling→reflex→rational, INV-052/T14)?',\\n            '   - Metaphor density appropriate to scene type?',\\n            '7. Document findings in beta-feedback/{N}/craft-lens.json with craft tool compliance per tool'\\n        ],\\n        'invariants': ['INV-038', 'INV-039', 'INV-040', 'INV-041', 'INV-042', 'INV-043', 'INV-044', 'INV-047', 'INV-051', 'INV-052', 'INV-053', 'INV-055', 'INV-060', 'INV-061', 'INV-062'],\\n        'artifact_reads': ['chapters/{N}/revised.md', 'chapters/{N}/metadata.json', 'craft-profile.json', 'foreshadowing-ledger.json'],\\n        'artifact_writes': ['beta-feedback/{N}/craft-lens.json'],\\n        'result_codes': ['completed', 'blocked'],\\n    },\\n\\n    'romantic-fantasy-writer-sensitivity-beta-reader': {\\n        'role': 'Evaluate chapter from sensitivity reader perspective: representation, harmful stereotypes, cultural sensitivity, power dynamics in romance, consent portrayal.',\\n        'process_steps': [\\n            '1. Read chapters/{N}/revised.md evaluating representation and sensitivity throughout',\\n            '2. Read characters/{CHAR-NNN}.json to understand character demographics and background',\\n            '3. Check representation:',\\n            '   - Are diverse characters present and three-dimensional (not token, not stereotype)?',\\n            '   - Do characters from non-dominant groups have agency per INV-008?',\\n            '   - Are disabilities, neurodivergence, mental health portrayed respectfully (if present)?',\\n            '4. Check for harmful tropes:',\\n            '   - Damsel in distress / lack of agency',\\n            '   - Magical minority fetishization',\\n            '   - \\\"Spicy\\\" trauma triggers used for heat without consent',\\n            '   - Stereotypical cultural practices',\\n            '   - Predatory/abusive behavior normalized as romance',\\n            '5. Check cultural sensitivity:',\\n            '   - If based on real-world cultures, accurate and respectful (not exoticized)?',\\n            '   - Magical/fantastical cultures described with specificity and respect?',\\n            '   - Religious/spiritual content treated respectfully?',\\n            '6. Check romance consent and power dynamics:',\\n            '   - Does romance include enthusiastic consent?',\\n            '   - Are power imbalances (employer/employee, master/student, captor/prisoner) addressed explicitly?',\\n            '   - Does intimate content respect boundaries and consent?',\\n            '7. Check for ableist language or assumptions',\\n            '8. Assess overall impact: would readers from marginalized groups feel represented and respected?',\\n            '9. Document findings in beta-feedback/{N}/sensitivity-lens.json with specific examples and context'\\n        ],\\n        'invariants': ['INV-008', 'INV-023'],\\n        'artifact_reads': ['chapters/{N}/revised.md', 'characters/{CHAR-NNN}.json'],\\n        'artifact_writes': ['beta-feedback/{N}/sensitivity-lens.json'],\\n        'result_codes': ['completed', 'blocked'],\\n    },\\n\\n    'romantic-fantasy-writer-originality-beta-reader': {\\n        'role': 'Evaluate chapter from originality perspective: flags passages/characters/plot elements/magic too similar to published works (INV-023 zero-tolerance). Checks style samples for transformative-only usage (INV-024).',\\n        'process_steps': [\\n            '1. Read chapters/{N}/revised.md thinking about published fantasy and romance works',\\n            '2. Flag any passage, character, plot element, or magic mechanic that resembles published works:',\\n            '   - Specific prose passages that are too similar in wording/structure',\\n            '   - Character archetypes that feel copied (with identifying details)',\\n            '   - Plot beats that mirror well-known stories (chosen one, love triangle, betrayal pattern)',\\n            '   - Magic systems that copy published rules without transformation',\\n            '3. For style sample usage (if present in story-config.json):',\\n            '   - Verify style-guide.json contains only abstract patterns (sentence rhythm, vocabulary register, etc.)',\\n            '   - Check prose doesn\\\\'t reproduce specific metaphors, turns of phrase, or distinctive patterns from samples',\\n            '   - Verify character archetypes aren\\\\'t borrowed whole from samples',\\n            '   - Verify plot beats aren\\\\'t in same sequence as samples (per INV-024)',\\n            '4. For any flagged similarity:',\\n            '   - Document the concerning passage or element',\\n            '   - Cite what published work it resembles',\\n            '   - Suggest differentiation (change the phrasing, the magic mechanics, the character detail)',\\n            '5. Assess overall originality:',\\n            '   - Is the story distinct from published comparable titles (comp titles from story-concept.json)?',\\n            '   - Does the story bring fresh elements to the romantic fantasy genre?',\\n            '   - Would readers recognize this as original work?',\\n            '6. Per INV-023 zero-tolerance: any critical plagiarism risk must be flagged as critical severity',\\n            '7. Document findings in beta-feedback/{N}/originality-lens.json'\\n        ],\\n        'invariants': ['INV-023', 'INV-024', 'INV-025'],\\n        'artifact_reads': ['chapters/{N}/revised.md', 'story-config.json', 'story-concept.json', 'style-guide.json'],\\n        'artifact_writes': ['beta-feedback/{N}/originality-lens.json'],\\n        'result_codes': ['completed', 'blocked'],\\n    },\\n\\n    'romantic-fantasy-writer-beta-synthesizer': {\\n        'role': 'Aggregate all five beta reader lens findings into a single prioritized list with severity levels and pass/fail verdict per INV-076.',\\n        'process_steps': [\\n            '1. Read all five beta-feedback/{N}/*.json files (romance, fantasy, craft, sensitivity, originality)',\\n            '2. Combine all findings into a single list: {originalIds, severity, category, description, requiredAction}',\\n            '3. De-duplicate findings that appear in multiple lenses (e.g., same pacing issue flagged by craft and fantasy readers)',\\n            '4. Sort by severity: critical first, major second, minor third',\\n            '5. Assess verdict per INV-076 \\\"Severity-Gated Acceptance\\\":',\\n            '   - If any critical findings: verdict = revision-required',\\n            '   - If major findings but no critical: verdict = revision-required',\\n            '   - If only minor findings and suggestions: verdict = accepted',\\n            '6. Write beta-synthesis/{N}.json with:',\\n            '   - Aggregated findings array',\\n            '   - Summary count (critical/major/minor)',\\n            '   - Revision priorities (ordered by severity and importance)',\\n            '   - Verdict (accepted|revision-required)',\\n            '   - Cross-lens agreement notes (e.g., \\\"Both craft and fantasy readers flagged pacing issue\\\")',\\n            '7. If revision-required: provide clear guidance on what to fix',\\n            '8. Include upstream references to all five lens reports (per INV-029)'\\n        ],\\n        'invariants': ['INV-013', 'INV-076'],\\n        'artifact_reads': ['beta-feedback/{N}/*'],\\n        'artifact_writes': ['beta-synthesis/{N}.json'],\\n        'result_codes': ['completed', 'blocked'],\\n    },\\n\\n    'romantic-fantasy-writer-polisher': {\\n        'role': 'Perform final proofread on accepted chapter: catch remaining typos, formatting issues, ensure publication readiness per INV-073. Create polished final version.',\\n        'process_steps': [\\n            '1. Read chapters/{N}/revised.md (or chapters/{N}/final.md if re-polishing)',\\n            '2. Conduct final proofread:',\\n            '   - Spelling, punctuation, grammar',\\n            '   - Consistent formatting (italics, em-dashes, scene breaks)',\\n            '   - Consistent capitalization and formatting of world-specific terms',\\n            '   - Paragraph breaks for readability (no walls of text)',\\n            '3. Check publication-ready prose quality per INV-073:',\\n            '   - Prose is lush but not purple (matches tone contract)',\\n            '   - Emotionally resonant but not melodramatic',\\n            '   - Genre-appropriate for romantic fantasy',\\n            '   - Professional quality throughout',\\n            '4. Verify chapter metadata is complete and accurate',\\n            '5. Double-check character names, place names against continuity tracker',\\n            '6. Final sense check: does chapter feel polished and ready for reader?',\\n            '7. Write chapters/{N}/final.md with frontmatter including: chapterNum, pov, wordCount, finalVersion, passedAllGates: true',\\n            '8. Write status.json with result=completed'\\n        ],\\n        'invariants': ['INV-073'],\\n        'artifact_reads': ['chapters/{N}/revised.md'],\\n        'artifact_writes': ['chapters/{N}/final.md'],\\n        'result_codes': ['completed', 'blocked'],\\n    },\\n\\n    'romantic-fantasy-writer-summary-generator': {\\n        'role': 'Generate chapter summary for series knowledge base: key events, character development, world changes, unresolved threads, romance progression.',\\n        'process_steps': [\\n            '1. Read chapters/{N}/final.md and extract key information',\\n            '2. Read characters/index.json to understand character arcs',\\n            '3. Document:',\\n            '   - Key events: major plot points in this chapter (2-5 bullet points)',\\n            '   - Character development: how each major character evolved/changed (per character)',\\n            '   - World changes: any new facts established about world (magic, politics, geography, culture)',\\n            '   - Romance progression: where the romance arc moved (stage, key moment, emotional shift)',\\n            '   - Unresolved threads: what questions/threads remain open for future chapters',\\n            '4. Write chapter-summaries/{N}.json with structured summary data',\\n            '5. Include upstream reference to final.md',\\n            '6. Keep summaries concise (3-5 sentences per section) for easy scanning'\\n        ],\\n        'invariants': ['INV-031'],\\n        'artifact_reads': ['chapters/{N}/final.md', 'characters/index.json'],\\n        'artifact_writes': ['chapter-summaries/{N}.json'],\\n        'result_codes': ['completed', 'blocked'],\\n    },\\n\\n    'romantic-fantasy-writer-delivery-assembler': {\\n        'role': 'Assemble complete delivery package: final chapter manuscript, summaries, series KB updates, quality metrics, delivery report.',\\n        'process_steps': [\\n            '1. Read all chapters/{N}/final.md files and compile into complete manuscript',\\n            '2. Read all chapter-summaries/{N}.json and compile summary index',\\n            '3. Read series-kb/index.json and verify it has been updated with this book\\\\'s content',\\n            '4. Calculate quality metrics:',\\n            '   - Total word count across all chapters',\\n            '   - Average chapter length',\\n            '   - Chapter count',\\n            '   - Craft tool compliance summary (which tools used, which chapters enforced each)',\\n            '   - Invariant adherence report (which invariants were tested, how many passed)',\\n            '   - Beta reader sentiment summary (average scores across lenses)',\\n            '   - Revision cycle count',\\n            '5. Create delivery-report.json with:',\\n            '   - storyId, totalWordCount, chapterCount',\\n            '   - qualityMetrics (as above)',\\n            '   - outstandingItems (only minor findings deferred per INV-076)',\\n            '   - seriesKBUpdated flag',\\n            '   - artifactManifest (list of all produced files)',\\n            '6. Verify all required artifacts exist and are valid JSON/markdown',\\n            '7. Package assembled materials for delivery to user (via guide)',\\n            '8. Write status.json with result=completed'\\n        ],\\n        'invariants': ['INV-031', 'INV-076'],\\n        'artifact_reads': ['chapters/{N}/final.md', 'chapter-summaries/{N}.json', 'series-kb/index.json'],\\n        'artifact_writes': ['delivery-report.json'],\\n        'result_codes': ['completed', 'blocked'],\\n    },\\n\\n    'romantic-fantasy-writer-continuity-tracker': {\\n        'role': 'Maintain running continuity document updated after every chapter draft. Tracks character locations, timeline, knowledge state, promises, and naming consistency.',\\n        'process_steps': [\\n            '1. On initial invocation: create empty continuity-tracker.json',\\n            '2. After each chapter draft: update tracker with new information:',\\n            '   a. Timeline: add events from this chapter with in-world timing',\\n            '   b. Character positions: update where each character is at chapter end',\\n            '   c. Character knowledge: record what facts each POV character learned',\\n            '   d. Active promises: track Chekhov\\\\'s gun elements (foreshadowing plants, subplots, questions)',\\n            '   e. Naming registry: confirm spellings, add new names as introduced',\\n            '3. Before chapter N+1 is drafted: provide continuity-tracker to drafter for reference',\\n            '4. Continuously verify consistency: no character contradictions, timeline makes sense',\\n            '5. Per INV-011: update tracker after EVERY chapter draft (required step)',\\n            '6. Read and cross-reference information-asymmetry-map.json and foreshadowing-ledger.json for consistency',\\n            '7. Maintain continuity-tracker.json as the single source of truth for world state across all chapters',\\n            '8. Append only — existing entries never deleted, only updated (status field can change open→resolved)'\\n        ],\\n        'invariants': ['INV-002', 'INV-011', 'INV-016', 'INV-056'],\\n        'artifact_reads': ['chapters/{N}/draft.md', 'information-asymmetry-map.json', 'foreshadowing-ledger.json'],\\n        'artifact_writes': ['continuity-tracker.json'],\\n        'result_codes': ['completed', 'blocked'],\\n    },\\n\\n    'romantic-fantasy-writer-series-kb-manager': {\\n        'role': 'Manage series-level knowledge base lifecycle: promote per-book facts to series level on completion, enforce append-mostly rule (INV-070), track unresolved threads for sequels (INV-071).',\\n        'process_steps': [\\n            '1. On first book: create series-kb/index.json with seriesId, books array (this book), empty crossBookFacts',\\n            '2. On completion of each book:',\\n            '   a. Read all world-bible/* files, characters/*, chapter-summaries/*',\\n            '   b. Identify facts that are series-relevant (will affect future books)',\\n            '   c. Add entries to crossBookFacts array with type (world/character/magic/timeline/naming/style)',\\n            '   d. Maintain naming conventions registry across books',\\n            '   e. Track unresolved threads in unresolvedThreads array',\\n            '3. For sequels:',\\n            '   a. Per INV-071: concept developer must address all unresolvedThreads (continue/resolve/drop)',\\n            '   b. Per INV-070: verify no established facts are silently retconned (append-mostly rule)',\\n            '   c. If retcon necessary: document narratively (unreliable narrator, new discovery) in series KB',\\n            '4. Maintain crossBookFacts as authoritative source: no cross-book contradictions',\\n            '5. Keep series KB organized by type for easy reference by sequel agents',\\n            '6. Update series KB only after full book completion (polish phase)',\\n            '7. Manage naming consistency across books — maintain canonical spellings'\\n        ],\\n        'invariants': ['INV-070', 'INV-071', 'INV-032'],\\n        'artifact_reads': ['world-bible/*', 'characters/*', 'chapter-summaries/*'],\\n        'artifact_writes': ['series-kb/index.json'],\\n        'result_codes': ['completed', 'blocked'],\\n    },\\n\\n    'romantic-fantasy-writer-craft-tracker': {\\n        'role': 'Cross-cutting craft knowledge agent: maintains foreshadowing ledger, mystery box inventory, emotional throughline, symbolic motif registry, knowledge matrix per INV-053/T15, INV-061/T23, INV-058/T20, INV-054/T16, INV-056/T18.',\\n        'process_steps': [\\n            '1. Maintain foreshadowing-ledger.json: before drafting each chapter, review open plants; during chapter draft, drafter notes new plants and payoffs; after chapter, verify completeness (payoff rate tracking)',\\n            '2. Maintain mystery-box-inventory.json: track active unresolved questions per chapter; ensure 3-7 boxes stay open (INV-061/T23); when question answered, open new one within 1-2 chapters',\\n            '3. Maintain emotional-throughline.json: after each chapter draft, record POV character emotional state; verify no character in same emotional state for 3+ consecutive chapters (INV-037/INV-058/T20)',\\n            '4. Maintain symbolic-motif-registry.json: if symbolic motifs assigned in plotting, track appearances per chapter; ensure density doesn\\\\'t exceed target; verify motifs escalate/transform with theme (INV-054/T16)',\\n            '5. Maintain information-asymmetry-map.json: after each chapter, update what reader/characters know; verify no accidental info leaks (character uses knowledge they don\\\\'t have); manage dramatic irony spacing (INV-056/T18)',\\n            '6. All trackers updated after chapter draft, before chapter moves to revision',\\n            '7. Provide updated trackers to next-phase agents (line editor, reviser, beta readers)',\\n            '8. Anti-laziness mandate: check every tracker comprehensively; don\\\\'t skip entries; verify completeness'\\n        ],\\n        'invariants': ['INV-037', 'INV-053', 'INV-054', 'INV-056', 'INV-058', 'INV-061'],\\n        'artifact_reads': ['chapters/{N}/draft.md', 'chapter-outlines/{N}.json', 'craft-profile.json'],\\n        'artifact_writes': ['foreshadowing-ledger.json', 'mystery-box-inventory.json', 'emotional-throughline.json', 'symbolic-motif-registry.json', 'information-asymmetry-map.json'],\\n        'result_codes': ['completed', 'blocked'],\\n    },\\n}\\n\\n# Auditor-specific configurations\\n\\nauditor_configs = {\\n    'romantic-fantasy-writer-concept-auditor': {\\n        'role': 'Audit story concept for genre promise (INV-001), thematic coherence, craft profile completeness, and scope alignment.',\\n        'gate_checklist': [\\n            '✓ Genre Promise (INV-001): Both fantasy and romance arcs present? Romance reaches HFN minimum?',\\n            '✓ Thematic Coherence (INV-036): 2-3 thematic pillars identified? Each pillar visible in worldbuilding, character arcs, plot?',\\n            '✓ Craft Profile (INV-069/INV-078): 5-8 tools selected? Minimum met? Each tool justified for this story?',\\n            '✓ Scope Consistency (INV-031): Concept specifies standalone vs series, chapter count estimate, tone, genre balance?',\\n            '✓ Premise Clarity: Refined premise distinct from raw input? One paragraph? Clear hook?',\\n        ],\\n        'antiLaziness_rules': [\\n            '1. READ the entire concept artifact, not just title fields — verify actual thematic descriptions, not just theme names',\\n            '2. TRACE each thematic pillar through worldbuilding and character design — don\\\\'t accept \\\"thematic\\\" without evidence',\\n            '3. VERIFY craft tool rationales: each selection must explain why this story needs this tool (not \\\"because it\\\\'s popular\\\")',\\n            '4. ZERO-FINDINGS-IS-SUSPICIOUS: if concept seems perfect with no issues, conduct a second pass specifically hunting for genre Promise weaknesses and theme underdevelopment',\\n            '5. CITE SPECIFIC EVIDENCE: every pass/fail finding must reference lines from the concept artifact or cross-referenced artifacts',\\n            '6. Your work will be audited — provide detailed gate reasoning that someone else can verify',\\n        ],\\n        'remediation_format': 'On failure, provide: (1) which gate item failed, (2) why it failed (specific evidence), (3) which artifact needs revision (story-concept.json, craft-profile.json, etc.), (4) specific remediation (add 3rd thematic pillar, justify tools 6-8, etc.)',\\n    },\\n\\n    'romantic-fantasy-writer-worldbuilding-auditor': {\\n        'role': 'Audit worldbuilding artifacts for internal consistency (INV-002), no info-dumping quality (INV-007), and cross-artifact alignment.',\\n        'gate_checklist': [\\n            '✓ Internal Consistency (INV-002): Geography aligns with culture (can people physically live where described)? Magic system doesn\\\\'t contradict world rules? Politics aligns with geography/culture?',\\n            '✓ Cross-File Consistency: No contradictions between world-bible/geography.json and culture.json (e.g., desert terrain but farming culture)? Magic rules respected in politics? History explains current politics?',\\n            '✓ Magic System Completeness: Hard magic has rules/costs? Soft magic doesn\\\\'t solve conflicts? Sanderson\\\\'s Law check (INV-048/T10)?',\\n            '✓ No Anachronisms (INV-018): Does culture level match technology/concepts described? No modern tech in medieval world without justification?',\\n            '✓ Foreshadowing Setup: Do world rules enable character arcs and plot? Magic accessible to characters who need it? Politics create romantic obstacles?',\\n        ],\\n        'antiLaziness_rules': [\\n            '1. CHECK EVERY WORLD-BIBLE FILE: don\\\\'t skim — read geography locations, culture descriptions, magic rule list, politics, history',\\n            '2. CROSS-REFERENCE: pick 5 random facts and verify they\\\\'re consistent across files (e.g., if geography says desert, culture should be desert-adapted)',\\n            '3. VERIFY MAGIC RULES: if hard magic claimed, list all rules and check no conflict resolution violates them',\\n            '4. ANACHRONISM HUNT: search for modern concepts (democracy, electricity, psychology terminology) — verify each is grounded in world',\\n            '5. ZERO-FINDINGS-IS-SUSPICIOUS: if all world-bible files seem perfect, you\\\\'ve missed something — conduct second pass on consistency across 3+ files',\\n            '6. PROVIDE SPECIFIC CONFLICTS: every inconsistency finding must cite the two conflicting statements and their files/line references',\\n        ],\\n        'remediation_format': 'On failure, provide: (1) which world-bible file(s) have issues, (2) specific contradictions (cite both statements), (3) which file needs revision, (4) remediation (revise magic costs, change culture to match geography, retcon historical event, etc.)',\\n    },\\n\\n    'romantic-fantasy-writer-character-auditor': {\\n        'role': 'Audit characters for voice distinctness (INV-003/INV-034), agency (INV-008), and arc coherence.',\\n        'gate_checklist': [\\n            '✓ Voice Distinctness (INV-003/INV-034): Each POV character recognizable in 3-4 sentences? Voice parameters (sentence length, vocab, metaphor, thought pattern) documented and distinct?',\\n            '✓ Character Agency (INV-008): Both romantic leads make active choices driving plot? No leads purely reactive? Support cast has agency in their own arcs?',\\n            '✓ Antagonist Motivation (INV-022): Antagonist has comprehensible motivations (not evil for evil\\\\'s sake)? Understands their own cause?',\\n            '✓ Romance Arc Setup: Vulnerability ladder defined (5-8 escalating moments)? Internal resistance mapped (50%+ internal obstacles)? Chemistry plausible?',\\n            '✓ Consistency: Relationships documented with evolution? Character knowledge mapped per arc stage?',\\n        ],\\n        'antiLaziness_rules': [\\n            '1. READ EVERY CHARACTER FILE: don\\\\'t sample — read all CHAR-NNN files for protagonists, ensemble, antagonist',\\n            '2. VOICE DISTINCTNESS TEST: pick 2 POV characters, generate 4-sentence examples from their voiceFingerprints, assess if you could distinguish them blind (you should be able to)',\\n            '3. AGENCY AUDIT: for each lead, list their active choices per act — if list is empty or 80% reactive, agency is weak',\\n            '4. MOTIVATION CHECK: for antagonist, write down their goal in one sentence — if you can\\\\'t write it or it\\\\'s \\\"chaos/evil,\\\" motivation is underdeveloped',\\n            '5. ZERO-FINDINGS-IS-SUSPICIOUS: if characters seem perfect, you\\\\'ve skipped the work — re-read all voice fingerprints against story-concept.json tone and verify they\\\\'re distinct enough for distinct prose',\\n            '6. CITE EVIDENCE: every finding must reference specific character files, specific voice parameters, specific plot choices',\\n        ],\\n        'remediation_format': 'On failure, provide: (1) which character(s) failed checks, (2) why (weak voice, insufficient agency, unclear motivation), (3) which character file needs revision, (4) remediation (expand voiceFingerprint, add active choice in Act 2, document antagonist motivation, etc.)',\\n    },\\n\\n    'romantic-fantasy-writer-plotting-auditor': {\\n        'role': 'Audit plotting for Chekhov\\\\'s gun (INV-006), pacing variation (INV-020), dual-arc alignment (INV-050), and craft tool application.',\\n        'gate_checklist': [\\n            '✓ Chekhov\\\\'s Gun (INV-006): Every introduced element either pays off or is marked unresolved-for-series? Foreshadowing ledger 1:1 plant-payoff?',\\n            '✓ Pacing Variation (INV-020): No 3+ consecutive chapters with same tension level? Peaks and valleys natural?',\\n            '✓ Dual-Arc Alignment (INV-050): Fantasy and romance beats interleaved per chapter? Neither arc disappears for 3+ chapters?',\\n            '✓ Stakes Escalation (INV-044/T6): Stakes increase through acts? Act 3 stakes greater than Act 1?',\\n            '✓ Craft Tool Consistency: Chapter outlines reflect selected craft tools? Scene structures (Goal-Conflict-Disaster if T1 selected)?',\\n        ],\\n        'antiLaziness_rules': [\\n            '1. MAP CHEKHOV\\\\'S GUNS: create a table of every significant element introduced (character secret, magical artifact, prophecy, relationship tension) — verify each has a payoff chapter or is tagged unresolved',\\n            '2. PACING VISUALIZATION: create a tension graph — if you see 3+ consecutive chapters at same level, that\\\\'s a failure',\\n            '3. DUAL-ARC AUDIT: create two columns (fantasy beats, romance beats) and fill per chapter — verify neither column has 3+ empty rows',\\n            '4. STAKES CHECK: read Act 1 and Act 3 — what\\\\'s at risk? Act 3 must be higher stakes',\\n            '5. CRAFT TOOL VERIFICATION: if T1 (Scene-Sequel) selected, sample 5 scenes in outline — verify each has Goal/Conflict/Disaster (or sequel counterpart)',\\n            '6. ZERO-FINDINGS-IS-SUSPICIOUS: if outline seems perfect, re-check Chekhov\\\\'s guns — most common failure is dangling threads',\\n        ],\\n        'remediation_format': 'On failure, provide: (1) which plot element(s) failed checks, (2) why (unresolved plant, flat pacing, missing beat), (3) which outline files need revision, (4) remediation (add payoff chapter, redistribute tension across chapters, resequence beats, apply craft structure, etc.)',\\n    },\\n\\n    'romantic-fantasy-writer-style-auditor': {\\n        'role': 'Audit style guide for prose quality floor (INV-017), voice consistency (INV-015), and craft tool application (voice fingerprints per INV-055/T17).',\\n        'gate_checklist': [\\n            '✓ Voice Fingerprints (INV-055/T17): Each POV character has measurable voice parameters? Distinctiveness verifiable?',\\n            '✓ Prose Quality Floor (INV-017): Quality thresholds documented (cliché max, adverb limits, passive voice limits)?',\\n            '✓ Tone Contract (INV-043/T5): Opening tonal promise documented? Tones to avoid listed?',\\n            '✓ Scene-Type Palettes: Different tone guidance for action vs romantic vs introspective scenes?',\\n            '✓ Style Sample Compliance (INV-024): If samples used, only abstract patterns documented (not specific content)?',\\n        ],\\n        'antiLaziness_rules': [\\n            '1. VERIFY FINGERPRINTS: for each POV character, read their voice fingerprint data — must be specific metrics (sentence length ranges, vocabulary register percentages, metaphor density), not vague descriptions',\\n            '2. DISTINCTIVENESS TEST: create 2 sample sentences for each POV using their fingerprint — if you could generate sentences that both PPV characters could claim, the fingerprint is too vague',\\n            '3. QUALITY FLOOR AUDIT: verify prose quality floor has numeric thresholds (max 2 clichés, <20% adverbs, <15% passive voice) — vague limits like \\\"reasonable\\\" are not acceptable',\\n            '4. TONE AUDIT: verify tone contract references opening chapters and sets expectations for later chapters',\\n            '5. STYLE SAMPLE VERIFICATION: if samples provided, re-check style-analyzer output and style-guide — verify NO direct metaphors, phrases, character archetypes, or plot patterns copied from samples (INV-024)',\\n            '6. ZERO-FINDINGS-IS-SUSPICIOUS: if style guide seems perfect, quality thresholds are probably too loose — tighten them or find edge cases',\\n        ],\\n        'remediation_format': 'On failure, provide: (1) which style guide sections failed, (2) why (vague fingerprint, missing quality thresholds, style sample content contamination), (3) which files need revision (style-guide.json, characters/*.json), (4) remediation (add numeric voice metrics, set quality thresholds, remove copied content, etc.)',\\n    },\\n\\n    'romantic-fantasy-writer-drafting-auditor': {\\n        'role': 'Audit chapter draft for outline adherence (INV-010), continuity (INV-011), and craft tool enforcement. Adversarial gate preventing weak chapters.',\\n        'gate_checklist': [\\n            '✓ Outline Adherence (INV-010): Chapter covers all scene beats from outline? POV consistent? Emotional arc realized?',\\n            '✓ Continuity (INV-011): Character positions, timeline, knowledge state match continuity tracker?',\\n            '✓ Sequential Production (INV-012): This chapter is N and previous chapter N-1 is complete?',\\n            '✓ No Info-Dumping (INV-007): No exposition paragraphs >1 paragraph before returning to scene?',\\n            '✓ Craft Tool Enforcement: Selected craft tools applied (Scene structure, dialogue function, tension, foreshadowing)?',\\n        ],\\n        'antiLaziness_rules': [\\n            '1. OUTLINE COMPARISON: read outline, read draft — check every scene goal is hit, every beat appears, POV never shifts accidentally',\\n            '2. CONTINUITY VERIFICATION: verify 5 facts from continuity tracker appear in chapter (character position, timeline progression, piece of knowledge) — if none, chapter might have continuity gaps',\\n            '3. CRAFT TOOL CHECK: for each selected craft tool, find evidence in this chapter — if tool is supposed to be \\\"drafting\\\" phase but you can\\\\'t find it in 3+ chapters, something is wrong',\\n            '4. EXPOSITION AUDIT: scan for \\\"pure exposition paragraphs\\\" (paragraphs of pure world description with no character, action, or dialogue) — if found, measure against INV-007 one-paragraph rule',\\n            '5. VOICE CONSISTENCY: sample dialogue and thoughts from POV character — do they match the voice fingerprint?',\\n            '6. ZERO-FINDINGS-IS-SUSPICIOUS: if chapter seems perfect, you\\\\'ve missed a craft tool application or a continuity detail — re-read the continuity tracker and spot-check 3 facts',\\n        ],\\n        'remediation_format': 'On failure, provide: (1) what failed checks (outline, continuity, craft), (2) specific failures (which scene was skipped, which craft tool not applied, which character position is wrong), (3) severity (critical/major), (4) remediation (redraft to match outline, fix character position, apply scene structure, remove exposition dump, etc.)',\\n    },\\n\\n    'romantic-fantasy-writer-revision-auditor': {\\n        'role': 'Audit revised chapter to verify all edits are traceable (INV-014) and revision completeness (INV-013) before proceeding to beta reading.',\\n        'gate_checklist': [\\n            '✓ Revision Traceability (INV-014): Every change cites which finding prompted it? Revision history in frontmatter?',\\n            '✓ Multi-Pass Completeness (INV-013): Did chapter go through all mandatory reviews (developmental, line, copy)?',\\n            '✓ Critical Findings Resolved: All critical findings from edits addressed?',\\n            '✓ Major Findings Addressed: All major findings addressed (or explicitly deferred as editorial choice)?',\\n            '✓ Prose Quality Improved: Revision improved prose quality per INV-017 standards?',\\n        ],\\n        'antiLaziness_rules': [\\n            '1. TRACEABILITY AUDIT: read frontmatter findingsAddressed array — count items; cross-check against developmental.json, line-edit.json, copy-edit.json combined finding count — should roughly match (all critical/major should be cited)',\\n            '2. FINDINGS RESOLUTION: pick 3 random critical findings and verify the revised chapter addresses them — search for the specific issues in the prose',\\n            '3. EDIT COMPLETENESS: verify all three edit reports exist (developmental, line, copy) — if any is missing, that phase wasn\\\\'t completed (INV-013)',\\n            '4. PROSE QUALITY: compare draft to revised on random pages — should show improvement in target areas (clarity, clichés removed, voice tightened)',\\n            '5. UNADDRESSED FINDINGS: scan for any critical/major findings in the edit reports that were NOT cited in findingsAddressed array — if found, they weren\\\\'t addressed',\\n            '6. ZERO-FINDINGS-IS-SUSPICIOUS: if all findings seem addressed with no issues, verify prose actually changed — don\\\\'t accept \\\"revision complete\\\" without evidence of actual changes',\\n        ],\\n        'remediation_format': 'On failure, provide: (1) which traceability/completeness checks failed, (2) specific issues (missing revision citations, unaddressed findings, incomplete edits), (3) which chapter file needs further revision, (4) remediation (add finding citations, re-edit to address remaining critical findings, etc.)',\\n    },\\n\\n    'romantic-fantasy-writer-beta-reading-auditor': {\\n        'role': 'Audit beta synthesis quality and chapter verdict accuracy. Verify five reader lenses ran independently and findings are comprehensive.',\\n        'gate_checklist': [\\n            '✓ Five Lenses Present (INV-068): Do all five beta-feedback files exist (romance, fantasy, craft, sensitivity, originality)?',\\n            '✓ Independence: Each lens produced independent findings (not just copying other lenses)?',\\n            '✓ Coverage: Are findings substantive across different aspects (genre, craft, representation, originality)?',\\n            '✓ Synthesis Quality: Does synthesis accurately aggregate findings (de-duplication correct, severity assessment fair)?',\\n            '✓ Verdict Accuracy: Is verdict (accepted/revision-required) correct per findings (critical/major findings → revision-required)?',\\n        ],\\n        'antiLaziness_rules': [\\n            '1. INDEPENDENCE CHECK: read each lens findings file — should have different issues flagged (not all just complaining about pacing). If all 5 files flag identical issues, readers might be copy-pasting instead of independent analysis',\\n            '2. COVERAGE AUDIT: skim all five files — should see different types of feedback (emotional satisfaction vs magic consistency vs prose quality vs representation vs originality). If all are similar topics, some reader is skipping their lens',\\n            '3. SYNTHESIS VERIFICATION: read synthesis file, then read original 5 files — verify synthesis accurately combined them (correct de-duplication, correct severity assessment)',\\n            '4. VERDICT CHECK: count critical + major findings in synthesis — if >0, verdict MUST be revision-required per INV-076. If 0, verdict should be accepted. Mismatch is failure',\\n            '5. SEVERITY ACCURACY: for 5 random findings, verify their severity in synthesis matches the original lens judgment — if downgraded without reason, that\\\\'s inaccurate synthesis',\\n            '6. ZERO-FINDINGS-IS-SUSPICIOUS: if all five readers had zero issues or all had only minor issues, second reader might be missing something — spot-check each lens file for comprehensiveness',\\n        ],\\n        'remediation_format': 'On failure, provide: (1) which audit checks failed, (2) why (missing reader lens, poor independence, inaccurate synthesis, wrong verdict), (3) which files need revision, (4) remediation (re-run missing reader, re-synthesize with more care, correct verdict to match findings, etc.)',\\n    },\\n}\\n\\n# Print agent configs as documentation\\nprint(\\\"✅ Agent configuration loaded successfully\\\")\\nprint(f\\\"Specialist agents: {len(agent_configs) - len(auditor_configs)}\\\")\\nprint(f\\\"Auditor agents: {len(auditor_configs)}\\\")\\nprint(f\\\"Total: {len(agent_configs)}\\\")\\n\\nEOFILE\\npython3 /tmp/rewrite_agents.py\\n\", \"description\": \"Load agent configurations for systematic rewriting\"}"
            }
          }
